r /> pg. 49: In the sidebox about playable bloodlines<br /> <br /> The other five are in the main body of the text:<br /> <br /> pg. 65 Three mortal witches submitted to the Lazarene Harbingers\u2019<br /> Embrace and revived Lamia\u2019s order as the Drakaina.<br /> pg. 70 Indeed, the Drakaina and their Nightshade Necromancy evolved from<br /> the Kindred study of Lilin witch mysticism.<br /> pg. 70 Developed by the Drakaina<br /> pg. 70 Although the Drakaina developed the Path, they don\u2019t<br /> hoard it \u2014 it\u2019s the Dark Mother\u2019s gift, to share with all<br /> who worship her. Any Bahari necromancer may learn<br /> it from a Drakaina teacher.<br /> <br /> Four of these instances are in the same page, pg. 70; the Drakaina themselves are not explained, unlike the Maeghar, and we know very little about them.<br /> <br /> So, are we supposed to just assume they are identical to Dark Ages' Lamiae, but without the Cappadocians around? Is that it?<br /> They are not explained in the Bloodlines section, nothing?<br /> <br /> If that's the case, I find it extremely... irritating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 04-07-2016, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:06:07-07:00","id":861356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861343#post861343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will assume you are not implying that I don't know how to find terms in a PDF. I guess this is your idea of a joke.<br /> <br /> There are 6 instances of the word 'Drakaina' in the book.<br /> pg. 49: In the sidebox about playable bloodlines<br /> <br /> The other five are in the main body of the text:<br /> <br /> pg. 65 Three mortal witches submitted to the Lazarene Harbingers\u2019<br /> Embrace and revived Lamia\u2019s order as the Drakaina.<br /> pg. 70 Indeed, the Drakaina and their Nightshade Necromancy evolved from<br /> the Kindred study of Lilin witch mysticism.<br /> pg. 70 Developed by the Drakaina<br /> pg. 70 Although the Drakaina developed the Path, they don\u2019t<br /> hoard it \u2014 it\u2019s the Dark Mother\u2019s gift, to share with all<br /> who worship her. Any Bahari necromancer may learn<br /> it from a Drakaina teacher.<br /> <br /> Four of these instances are in the same page, pg. 70; the Drakaina themselves are not explained, unlike the Maeghar, and we know very little about them.<br /> <br /> So, are we supposed to just assume they are identical to Dark Ages' Lamiae, but without the Cappadocians around? Is that it?<br /> They are not explained in the Bloodlines section, nothing?<br /> <br /> If that's the case, I find it extremely... irritating.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I wasn't making an attempt at a joke. I had no prior knowledge of your knowing how to search a document, but now I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:30:49-07:00","id":861372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=860890#post860890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are your thoughts on the various cults that make up the Hand, and the Harbingers of Skulls' involvement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most if not all of them are interesting and readily usable by themselves even divorced from the greater sect. I'm wondering if the ROEG will not replace the Sabbat in my games as it doesn't strain my suspension of disbelief so much as the sword of Caine. The Ancient Lawgivers are perfect as an official answer to Sabbat' theology<br /> <br /> While the Harbinger of Skulls' membership is a bit jarring as they have good reason to hate their founder with a deadly passion, the implication the Capuchin converted most of them to &quot;becoming Onceborns&quot; is nice.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:36:46-07:00","id":861417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=860890#post860890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are your thoughts on the various cults that make up the Hand, and the Harbingers of Skulls' involvement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having not read this new book...I think it seems like a pretty cool idea! Of course, I've always liked the idea of the Hand having various factions and cults within it. And having the Harbingers there only makes sense...at least to me anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861299#post861299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot for these!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're very welcome!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861299#post861299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you taking requests already, if I can be so bold?<br /> <br /> I'd love to see a Tal'Mahe'Ra themed character sheet for mortal Indran mages! And perhaps ghouls/chatterlings, since these are so important to the sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll add it to my list...and see whats involved once I make my way though the book. The Ghoul/Chatterling one probably won't be too involved(or too different from my current Ghoul Sheet). The Mage one might be interesting, since if you wanted to match with the current Black hand sheet I'd have to rebuild the Mage sheet with the V20 aesthetics...<br /> <br /> But I'll add it to the list. Send me an email about it sometime...if you think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T17:46:30-07:00","id":861460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861158#post861158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving the book so far, but I have discovered a particularly irritating... thing, as I don't know whether it is intended as a feature or not.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of references to bloodlines that don't seem to be defined anywhere, specially the Drakaina. Can anyone help with this particular topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Found the same problem, and I wonder if it isn't just a typo to put them in the bloodlines column. They seems to be a resurgence of Lamia's cult of Lilith, a spiritual iteration, not a physical one. But could the Harbinger create anew a modern version of the Lamia, I'm not so sure...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","name":"Darthpalpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7454_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:23:28-07:00","id":861487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861158#post861158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving the book so far, but I have discovered a particularly irritating... thing, as I don't know whether it is intended as a feature or not.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of references to bloodlines that don't seem to be defined anywhere, specially the Drakaina. Can anyone help with this particular topic?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, they didn't make the cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:36:21-07:00","id":861540,"title":"","content":"Could this not be simply amended with a simple (for characteristics, see &quot;Lamia&quot; in V20 p...) ? Because as it is now, it's a little more than disturbing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","name":"Darthpalpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7454_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T20:21:42-07:00","id":861558,"title":"","content":"I'm going to wait for DriveThrurRPG to release the printed version, but I'm really happy Enoch was rediscovered. It was one of the most interesting things about the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:10:15-07:00","id":861626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861487#post861487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sadly, they didn't make the cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, and what does that mean? Will we see them defined in another book? Maybe in Lore of the Bloodlines or Dark Ages Companion? Or will they be removed from the text? Or will they be left as a teaser, a footnote, and nothing more?<br /> <br /> And thanks for giving me a somewhat straight answer and not telling me to use CTRL+F.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:17:45-07:00","id":861629,"title":"","content":"I love the amount of new info on the Baali that is scattered around the book, but I would prefer to have it all in a single place, the same way they did with the Harbingers, the Nagaraja and the Old Clan Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:48:54-07:00","id":861686,"title":"","content":"First of all, I love the book! I particulary like the elegant explanation of the mystery of the identity of the Capuchin. Well done!<br /> <br /> One thing I am a bit confused of is the similarities between a group called the Gardeners and the Royal Order of the Edenic Groundskeepers. The Gardeners have some kind of relation to Mithras childe Cretheus, while The Groundskeepers have a relation to Marcus Verus, another childe of Mithras. In both cases, there are talk about their childer:<br /> <br /> On page 23: The Western Hand was (and is, to these nights) comprised of three disparate fingers \u2014 the True Brujah, the Ventrue childer of Marcus Verus, and the Old Clan Tzimisce<br /> <br /> On page 25: \u201cWe are in the world, and of it,\u201d came the impassioned plea from the childer of Cretheus, spoken in a dozen different ways. \u201cAllow us to walk in the streets of our grandsires.\u201d<br /> <br /> Is there a mixup here? Is it supposed to be the same childe of Mithras in these 2 cases? Is there a relation between the Gardeners and the Groundskeepers?<br /> <br /> /Ho Dracon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/390-ho-dracon","name":"Ho Dracon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar390_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:29:01-07:00","id":861700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ho Dracon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861686#post861686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, I love the book! I particulary like the elegant explanation of the mystery of the identity of the Capuchin. Well done!<br /> <br /> One thing I am a bit confused of is the similarities between a group called the Gardeners and the Royal Order of the Edenic Groundskeepers. The Gardeners have some kind of relation to Mithras childe Cretheus, while The Groundskeepers have a relation to Marcus Verus, another childe of Mithras. In both cases, there are talk about their childer:<br /> <br /> On page 23: The Western Hand was (and is, to these nights) comprised of three disparate fingers \u2014 the True Brujah, the Ventrue childer of Marcus Verus, and the Old Clan Tzimisce<br /> <br /> On page 25: \u201cWe are in the world, and of it,\u201d came the impassioned plea from the childer of Cretheus, spoken in a dozen different ways. \u201cAllow us to walk in the streets of our grandsires.\u201d<br /> <br /> Is there a mixup here? Is it supposed to be the same childe of Mithras in these 2 cases? Is there a relation between the Gardeners and the Groundskeepers?<br /> <br /> /Ho Dracon</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like the direction of the Capuchin! Of course, while it solves one Capuchin mystery, it opens others. <br /> <br /> Regarding Verus and Cretheus - Verus is suspecting the existence of the TBH due to his activity in the Edenic Groundskeepers. For a Methuselah he's very active, but since his bond to his sire broke about two decades ago, it's understandable he may have decided to leave the British Isles for a change. <br /> <br /> I've asked Neall to pop into the thread about Cretheus. I have a feeling that the Western Hand is populated by Cret's childer, but he may be able to clarify.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T04:02:39-07:00","id":861730,"title":"","content":"Those of you who buy a copy of the book, I ask you give it a review - even as short as a single paragraph - on DriveThruRPG. Rating a book and reviewing it, in both the positive and the negative, allows more people to determine whether this is a book they'd be interested in buying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T04:06:00-07:00","id":861733,"title":"","content":"The quality of this book makes me wish even more that there was a V20 Inconnu. To complete the pair. With all the factions. Hunedora, Conspiracies, Capadocius, Golgonda, Monitors, Influences upon the Paths and indirect politics (unable to take positions). improvement of systems and secret knowledge (as of Ordo Dracul), technology enthusiasts and ways to improve the condition, recruitment and lighting services. In addition to possibilities of play of the Roman Empire to the Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> Camarilla Guide, Sabbat, cities and independent territories and a &quot;Justicars and cardinals.&quot; It would be all that would ask more for the V20. In addition to what has already been published, it is now about to be published and what I quoted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T04:34:41-07:00","id":861737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861733#post861733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The quality of this book makes me wish even more that there was a V20 Inconnu. To complete the pair. With all the factions. Hunedora, Conspiracies, Capadocius, Golgonda, Monitors, Influences upon the Paths and indirect politics (unable to take positions). improvement of systems and secret knowledge (as of Ordo Dracul), technology enthusiasts and ways to improve the condition, recruitment and lighting services. In addition to possibilities of play of the Roman Empire to the Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> Camarilla Guide, Sabbat, cities and independent territories and a &amp;quot;Justicars and cardinals.&amp;quot; It would be all that would ask more for the V20. In addition to what has already been published, it is now about to be published and what I quoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post this on the Monday blog! Rich may well take notice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T04:48:47-07:00","id":861744,"title":"","content":"A very good book and a nice update/clean up of the Tal'Mahe'Ra. The Capuchin &quot;revelation&quot; alone is worth the price and all the nice call-back to the previous lore element that were developped after DSotBH and added to the &quot;current&quot; Tal'Mahe'Ra without feeling shoehorned. Very, an excellent job at organically updating the setting.<br /> Oh, and the Soul Eater... err, Asakku, make a lot more sense, even if (or because) it downplay the Werewolf cosmology in Vampire.<br /> <br /> My only real gripe is : no mention of the Kuei-Jin. When speaking of the (Far)-Eastern Hand, no mention. The manipulations of the Hand in India doesn't have any information about of the Kuei-Jin situation there. No wink on the fact that the Nagaraja will find asylum in the Green Court after the 6GM. I know that many doesn't like them, but a sidebar would have been nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2140,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","user":"Asimar","date":". 04-08