actions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T01:38:44-07:00","id":862520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862503#post862503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Responsible book V20 Black Hand, David Hill, has said he does not like Kuei Jins.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And it really seems to me that they are not well Cysts by anyone from the publisher at the time, but there is already guessing mine. Especially because the concept has suffered accusations of being racist.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I was also developer on V20 Dark Ages. <br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with my opinions on KotE. I didn't write the book; I developed it. It's not as if my writers wrote a bunch of references to it, and I cut them. They just didn't write about them, and I didn't feel as if we really needed to change that. I feel it's a pretty tight book, and adding more directions might have muddied the waters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T06:22:08-07:00","id":862570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862292#post862292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Au contraire, mon frere. You'll find a Lamiae presence within the Bahari, and the Harbingers of Skulls are <i>very </i>present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course! forgot the Harbingers of Skulls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T07:20:07-07:00","id":862578,"title":"","content":"From those who have read the book: how likely is someone who <b><i>loathed</i></b> what Hill did with DA bloodlines and Koldunic Sorcery to find this sourcebook palatable? I was a big fan of <i>DSotBH</i>, but between snippets I've read about these elements and being reminded that the developer whose ideas and execution I disagree with the most was in charge of this project, I'm suddenly much more dubious about buying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T08:31:09-07:00","id":862589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862578#post862578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From those who have read the book: how likely is someone who <b><i>loathed</i></b> what Hill did with DA bloodlines and Koldunic Sorcery to find this sourcebook palatable? I was a big fan of <i>DSotBH</i>, but between snippets I've read about these elements and being reminded that the developer whose ideas and execution I disagree with the most was in charge of this project, I'm suddenly much more dubious about buying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't sound easy, but I think that the book does a fairly good job at bridging the differences between DA20 and V20, so I would try to suspend my judgement and read the book before dismissing it as loathsome.<br /> <br /> In addition, I am unsure about what you mean with 'what someone did with DA bloodlines and Koldunic Sorcery'. What do you mean, more specifically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 04-10-2016, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T10:20:50-07:00","id":862640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862570#post862570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course! forgot the Harbingers of Skulls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, that unplayable mini-clan of 50 elder Cappadocians that, as written, is unplayable in a normal game. Why do we need material on them again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T10:41:45-07:00","id":862652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862640#post862640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes, that unplayable mini-clan of 50 elder Cappadocians that, as written, is unplayable in a normal game. Why do we need material on them again?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are Antagonists for most factions.... No, ALL factions (Sabbat included).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T11:18:23-07:00","id":862667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862640#post862640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes, that unplayable mini-clan of 50 elder Cappadocians that, as written, is unplayable in a normal game. Why do we need material on them again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Harbingers are very much playable. One of my favourite bloodlines. Have a read of the sourcebook and let me know your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","user":"The Gentleman Gamer","date":". 04-09-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T11:50:19-07:00","id":862675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862667#post862667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Harbingers are very much playable. One of my favourite bloodlines. Have a read of the sourcebook and let me know your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have the black hand book, so just going by the core:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Harbingers are alleged to all be elders</b>, and frighteningly powerful. While their sudden appearance suggests a long bout of torpor, they don't behave like recently-awakened vampires. Indeed, they claim they have been dead these past five centuries. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The background of a &quot;typical&quot; Harbinger is impossible to know. <b>They are all elders</b>, and who they were in life has been lost to time. </div> </div> </div>Revenge-obsessed elder vampire necromancer is a concept that fits an extremely small number of games. Hell, &quot;elder vampire&quot; is a concept that fits an extremely small number of games. And getting past the &quot;they are all elders&quot; part, I just don't see the point. Angry necromancer is great idea, but you don't need an entire clan of them. Any vampire at all can fit into the &quot;angry necromancer&quot; concept. While players frequently have a &quot;my concept is my clan&quot; problem, where they are playing a stereotypical Tremere/Ventrue/Brujah, White Wolf writers have an opposite problem: &quot;my clan is my character's concept&quot;. Marconius is a tinker-bell vampire, so he's a member of the clan of tinker-bell vampires, Daughters of Cacophony are a clan of vampire singers, and so on. There'd probably be a clan dedicated to basketweaving if nWoD hadn't killed the company.<br /> What do Harbingers of Skulls <i>as a clan </i>bring to the table that can not be trivially expressed by a <i>character</i> of any other clan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T11:58:52-07:00","id":862679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862675#post862675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do Harbingers of Skulls <i>as a clan </i>bring to the table that can not be trivially expressed by a <i>character</i> of any other clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are talking about a ghost world campaign thing (check the previous posts). I guess it has something to do with the harbies...It still sounds silly, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:18:06-07:00","id":862688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862679#post862679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are talking about a ghost world campaign thing (check the previous posts). I guess it has something to do with the harbies...It still sounds silly, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any ghost-related plot hits the wall of the game's primary PC faction having zero necromancer clans. When there's something strange in your neighborhood, you politely ignore it because you don't have a clan that interacts with ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:48:35-07:00","id":862708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862688#post862688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When there's something strange in your neighborhood, you politely ignore it because you don't have a clan that interacts with ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my point.<br /> Harbies and Giovanni are a real thorn for the factions. Having them fight each-other wasn't enough. Maybe having them distracted with a ghost-world might give some more space for non-ghost-related plots.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:13:26-07:00","id":862723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862578#post862578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From those who have read the book: how likely is someone who <b><i>loathed</i></b> what Hill did with DA bloodlines and Koldunic Sorcery to find this sourcebook palatable? I was a big fan of <i>DSotBH</i>, but between snippets I've read about these elements and being reminded that the developer whose ideas and execution I disagree with the most was in charge of this project, I'm suddenly much more dubious about buying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I HATED the flavor changes of VDA20 (but liked the koldunic kraina and some mechanical changes), but GttTMR have struck a nice balance between updating and keeping the feel of the original book. The two books almost stand at opposite, flavorwise. Talk about a polarizing developper <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then again, just my two cent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:43:23-07:00","id":862742,"title":"","content":"The write up of the Harbingers of Skulls let them be playable by saying the line got into a recruiting frenzy to help them understand the modern world. there are Lazarene fledglings now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:52:06-07:00","id":862746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862742#post862742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> there are Lazarene fledglings now.</div> </div> </div> </div>...shit - uh, I mean, which faction? Black Hand only? or Sabbat too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:30:53-07:00","id":862755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862675#post862675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't have the black hand book, so just going by the core:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Revenge-obsessed elder vampire necromancer is a concept that fits an extremely small number of games. Hell, &quot;elder vampire&quot; is a concept that fits an extremely small number of games. And getting past the &quot;they are all elders&quot; part, I just don't see the point. Angry necromancer is great idea, but you don't need an entire clan of them. Any vampire at all can fit into the &quot;angry necromancer&quot; concept. While players frequently have a &quot;my concept is my clan&quot; problem, where they are playing a stereotypical Tremere/Ventrue/Brujah, White Wolf writers have an opposite problem: &quot;my clan is my character's concept&quot;. Marconius is a tinker-bell vampire, so he's a member of the clan of tinker-bell vampires, Daughters of Cacophony are a clan of vampire singers, and so on. There'd probably be a clan dedicated to basketweaving if nWoD hadn't killed the company.<br /> What do Harbingers of Skulls <i>as a clan </i>bring to the table that can not be trivially expressed by a <i>character</i> of any other clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're focusing a little too much on the stereotype as concept. Just as not every Ventrue is a stockbroker, and not every Brujah is a punk, not every Harbinger is a revenge-obsessed elder vampire. As they're a bloodline, they've had less exposure and therefore less opportunity for exploration of different concepts. Let's break it down.<br /> <br /> <b>Revenge-obsessed:</b> You only need play this part of the concept if you're playing a Harbinger in the Japheth contingent (as described in the True Black Hand book) as they joined the Sabbat and began plotting against the Giovanni for reasons both real and imagined. Now, you're going by the core - which is fine - but even then an individual Harbinger isn't forced by his Sabbat pack to wage war on the Giovanni. That's very much a Harbinger trait, and one they can take or leave.<br /> <br /> <b>Elder: </b>Harbingers of Skulls as a bloodline are dominated by elders, it's true, but the True Black Hand book states they've been newly Embracing due to their acknowledgement of being out-of-touch with the world today. You don't have to play an elder Harbinger if you want to play one of their modern childer. It's left nebulous when they began Embracing, so I'd give leeway of up to 40 years prior to today, off the top of my head. Again, you're going off of the core book, so you can still play a Harbinger - they were Embraced very shortly prior to their enforced 500 year &quot;torpor.&quot; When they wake in the modern nights they're still fledglings.<br /> <br /> <b>Necromancer: </b>Harbingers are necromancers, their line having spent a great deal of time in the Shadowlands and making deals with wraiths for survival. If a necromancer concept doesn't fit your chronicle then that's fine - be a Harbinger with focus in Fortitude. The Clan that spawned them may have been predominantly Necromancy/Mortis-driven, but just as with every other line, they have two other Disciplines. It is possible to survive in the Shadowlands without Necromancy as a Discipline. It's difficult, but possible; if you have Allies, Contacts, maybe a Mentor, and Retainers. My point is if your group doesn't interact with ghosts, zombies, or Giovanni, you can still play a character of Harbinger origins without feeling useless. Then - on the rare occasion you <i>do</i> use Necromancy - it becomes a fun novelty rather than an expected trick.<br /> <br /> <b>Angry Necromancer: </b>I believe the number of Harbingers is now well over 50, but that may be from somewhere in my notes. Either way, not every Harbinger of Skulls is angry. The bloodline do feel wronged by someone, or some group, but they don't exist in a permanent state of anger. Think of the coolly calculating necromancers, the voyeuristic oracles, the burly graverobbers, and fanatical death cultists among them. They all pursue their own purposes, and maybe each feel betrayal, but they're not possessed by it.<br /> <br /> <b>My Clan is my character's concept: </b>I agree that a lot of people play bloodlines - the Harbingers not excepted here - so they can play something weird and wonderful, matching exactly the bloodline stereotype. I don't think there's anything wrong with this if players and Storytellers enjoy it. I had a player who played a slave Gargoyle and loved it. People do the exact same things with the Clans. I've had players look at the Clan section of the book first, see Vykos, and want to play a fleshcrafting-obsessed Tzimisce forevermore. For those who don't, these bloodlines can spawn as many character concepts as any Clan. Want to play a Harbinger stockbroker recently Embraced so his sire can recoup his lost fortune? A Kiasyd pack priest dedicated to forging a new Path of Enlightenment? Daughter of Cacophony bio-weapons engineer who lacks a singing voice but can make a dirty bomb with a paperclip and rubber band? What you're describing are player decisions, not helped by narrow descriptions that were necessary when the bloodline was written - they're each a strict subset of an existing line, after all. Clans have the same issue, but have benefited from expansion across over a hundred books. Bloodlines give players a chance to forge their own backgrounds and create their own innovative concepts while playing with a part of the game they particularly enjoy.<br /> <br /> <b>What do Harbingers bring to the table that any other Clan can't: </b>I feel you could apply this question to any Clan or bloodline. Toreador are artists. Malkavians are mad. Tremere are a blood magic pyramid. Harbingers are revenge-obsessed necromancers. Yes - that description is tighter, because they're a bloodline. But by unpacking that stereotype you have concepts such as &quot;Ancient vampire lost in a time he doesn't recognise,&quot; &quot;Fledgling Embraced to educate her master,&quot; &quot;Committed destroyer of all Giovanni plans,&quot; &quot;Cold, calculating, eschatologist,&quot; &quot;Seeker of the mysteries surrounding his line's fall,&quot; &quot;Fanatical student of the Path of Death and the Soul,&quot; &quot;Spy who uses the Shadowlands as his spotting post,&quot; &quot;Dedicant to restoring her Clan,&quot; &quot;Harbinger diplomat to the Camarilla,&quot; and so on.<br /> <br /> If a player wanted me to describe what the Harbingers have that no other Clan possesses, I would say they're a group of vampires who lost time. No other Clan has &quot;history&quot; as an intrinsic stereotype. They weren't around to witness 500+ years of technological and cultural development, forcing them in these nights to quickly adapt or die. I could well see a Harbinger exposing himself to as much media as possible in an effort to remain relevant. A band of vampires childlike in their naivete about the modern world is a lot of fun to my mind.<br /> <br /> With all that said, I'm actually now going to alter my next chronicle to incorporate these betrayed necromancers; dangerous in power, but utterly fearful of the world they find themselves thrust into.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:35:06-07:00","id":862758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862708#post862708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's my point.<br /> Harbies and Giovanni are a real thorn for the factions. Having them fight each-other wasn't enough. Maybe having them distracted with a ghost-world might give some more space for non-ghost-related plots.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> ...shit - uh, I mean, which faction? Black Hand only? or Sabbat too?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I could well see a Harbinger who was once.. oo.. a chamberlain to a Prince in the Dark Ages wanting to get back onto the political ladder and ignoring all that Giovanni nonsense. In fact, one part of V20 True Black Hand says they're acknowledging their Giovanni vendetta's futility.<br /> <br /> The bloodline is in part harboured by the True Black Hand, but as their writer, I'm comfortable that it's not just the TBH-aligned Harbingers who would have begun Embracing since their emergence. Look out for deathmask-wearing vampires in Elysium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:44:26-07:00","id":862769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Harbingers of Skulls as a bloodline are dominated by elders, it's true, but the True Black Hand book states they've been newly Embracing due to their acknowledgement of being out-of-touch with the world today. </div> </div> </div>So the corebook is lying and you are retconning things. Got it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>My Clan is my character's concept:</b> </div> </div> </div>You didn't get it. I'm talking about the book writers making clans around the concept of a unique character they introduced. Like Marconius and Kyasid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No other Clan has &quot;history&quot; as an intrinsic stereotype. They weren't around to witness 500+ years of technological and cultural development, forcing them in these nights to quickly adapt or die. </div> </div> </div>I... what? What about all the elder vampires in torpor? What about the common stereotype of an elder who doesn't get computers and still thinks those newfangled horseless carriages should be banned? Tremere elders are debating whether Path of Technomancy is a legitimate use of Thaumaturgy or if they should just burn the witch. &quot;The modern world is alien to me&quot; is elder vampire 101.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:51:56-07:00","id":862775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862769#post862769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the corebook is lying and you are retconning things. Got it.<br /> <br /> <br /> You didn't get it. I'm talking about the book writers making clans around the concept of a unique character they introduced. Like Marconius and Kyasid.<br /> <br /> <br /> I... what? What about all the elder vampires in torpor? What about the common stereotype of an elder who doesn't get computers and still thinks those newfangled horseless carriages should be banned? Tremere elders are debating whether Path of Technomancy is a legitimate use of Thaumaturgy or if they should just burn the witch. &quot;The modern world is alien to me&quot; is elder vampire 101.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! No, the core book isn't lying and I'm not retconning anything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What this book is doing is expanding the line, just as Lore of the Clans (and the Clanbooks of old) expanded their Clans. There's nothing wrong with keeping the original concept if you want it, but if you don't, you have some options presented to you in True Black Hand.<br /> <br /> I believe the Kiasyd were introduced before Marconius as a method of have &quot;fae-touched vampires.&quot; There is no prototypical Harbinger, at any rate. Though if bloodlines do form around one particularly powerful vampire who breaks off his own line, I'd say it makes sense that that vampire - Marconius, for instance - is different to normal Lasombra, and his childer more strongly resemble him than his original line. I've seen so many Kiasyd played now. They do seem to be one of the favourite bloodlines, next to Samedi.<br /> <br /> The missing half a millennium is important to the Harbinger background, if you wish to use it, which is why it's a big part of their concept. I don't think any other bloodline or Clan has that stereotype in-built in their line. I'd be interested in hearing your thoughts on how any other Clan has such a unique concept that it can't be played by a vampire of any other Clan, but as that's not related to this book, feel free to PM me or start a new thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:54:50-07:00","id":862855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862758#post862758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could well see a Harbinger who was once.. oo.. a chamberlain to a Prince in the Dark Ages wanting to get back onto the political ladder and ignoring all that Giovanni nonsense. In fact, one part of V20 True Black Hand says they're acknowledging their Giovanni vendetta's futility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like the Story's moving forward. I doubt Unre would go along with that...not that she was in agreement with other Lazarenes in the first place.<br /> Maybe this is the right time for her to stop messing with the Sabbat and realize Myca didn't become Sascha for nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:24:39-07:00","id":862928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862675#post862675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't have the black hand book, so just going by the core:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Revenge-obsessed elder vampire necromancer is a concept that fits an extremely small number of games. Hell, &quot;elder vampire&quot; is a concept that fits an extremely small number of games. And getting past the &quot;they are all elders&quot; part, I just don't see the point. Angry necromancer is great idea, but you don't need an entire clan of them. Any vampire at all can fit into the &quot;angry necromancer&quot; concept. While players frequently have a &quot;my concept is my clan&quot; problem, where they are playing a stereotypical Tremere/Ventrue/Brujah, White Wolf writers have an opposite problem: &quot;my clan is my character's concept&quot;. Marconius is a tinker-bell vampire, so he's a member of the clan of tinker-bell vampires, Daughters of Cacophony are a clan of vampire singers, and so on. There'd probably be a clan dedicated to basketweaving if nWoD hadn't killed the company.<br /> What do Harbingers of Skulls <i>as a clan </i>bring to the table that can not be trivially expressed by a <i>character</i> of any other clan?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Good news! They are written up strongly in a book that pretty much expects you to play some level of Elder. Unlike your average Cam, or Sabbat game your average True Hand Game is about playing some level of Elder with Neonates being the bizare exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:13:04-07:00","id":862976,"title":"","content":"My personal opinion: While it's true that the stereotype of elder vampires is that they're perpetually stuck in whatever age they died in, and certainly many are, it shouldn't be held as a universal truth applicable to all. Just like we have a lot of elder humans who make the effort to learn technology and thrive in an age way more advanced than the one they grew up in, there are elder vampires who will also make the effort because they see advantages in doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:01:24-07:00","id":863013,"title":"","content":"I mean..you really can't tell the writers they're wrong. They did write the clans/bloodlines and it is published. So it's pretty much Canon now. You don't agree with it. Change it for your games. Pretty simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:59:46-07:00","id":863037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862755#post862755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're focusing [...] they find themselves thrust into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dear Sir:<br /> <br /> This is one of the best posts I have read in this Forums in ages. You are now, officially, one of my favourite Onyx Path writers. Not only one of the best posts ever, but also one of the best answers ever.<br /> <br /> Amazing and incredible. Truly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T23:06:18-07:00","id":863041,"title":"","content":"Will there be information on why the Kyasid and the Maeghar split in Lore of the Bloodlines? I'm loving the three way relationship between Maeghar, DA-Kiasyd and V20-Kiasyd. I understood it was Marconius desire to create a &quot;legitimate&quot; bloodline...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T01:43:23-07:00","id":863074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863037#post863037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dear Sir:<br /> <br /> This is one of the best posts I have read in this Forums in ages. You are now, officially, one of my favourite Onyx Path writers. Not only one of the best posts ever, but also one of the best answers ever.<br /> <br /> Amazing and incredible. Truly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for saying so. I'm a firm believer that bloodlines offer exciting diversity to those who want it. If the stereotype doesn't fit a chronicle, then don't play it, or play a character from the bloodline who isn't defined by his bloodline - it's as simple as that. <br /> <br /> All vampires are humans first, with the range of human positive and negative traits; emotionally, physically, and through personality. The bloodline is just an added layer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T01:45:05-07:00","id":863075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863041#post863041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be information on why the Kyasid and the Maeghar split in Lore of the Bloodlines? I'm loving the three way relationship between Maeghar, DA-Kiasyd and V20-Kiasyd. I understood it was Marconius desire to create a &amp;quot;legitimate&amp;quot; bloodline...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kiasyd in Lore of the Bloodlines are very much Marconius', but that doesn't mean they won't comment on tales of aberrant Embraced changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T03:56:44-07:00","id":863099,"title":"","content":"Lots of really good stuff in here. I particularly like the Itarajan Sorcery. I was a little sad to not get a splat for Molochim Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1456-zeke-hubris","name":"Zeke Hubris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T05:25:24-07:00","id":863113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863041#post863041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be information on why the Kyasid and the Maeghar split in Lore of the Bloodlines?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote both the DA and BH Kiasyd, so I'd like to chime in here. Keep in mind that until/if it appears in the books, this is **all my headcanon**.<br /> <br /> My idea for the DA Kiasyd was prompted by all the mysteries and conflicting stories surrounding the modern Kiasyd, as well as the idea that fae/changelings were more prevalent pre-enlightenment. So I broadened the Kiasyd concept from Marconius and his 7-foot tall blue peeps, to all fae-touched vampires. The DA book didn't offer glimpses into the future so there was no way to outright connect them to the V20 Kiasyd, but I did leave some bread crumbs (like Marconius' claim that he was once a Lasombra and re-created himself through sorcery).<br /> <br /> Fast-forward to the BH book, where David and I felt the &quot;Maeghar&quot; would fit in perfectly. They're fae-touched, have seemingly suffered overwhelming loss (which makes them a great for the TMR) and are cloaked in secrecy (ditto). They also have a &quot;stay away from Marconius&quot; attitude.<br /> <br /> Given what we know about vampires in general (ruthless, broke no competition) and Lasombra-if-Marconius-was-one in particular (complete asshats), we probably know &quot;why&quot; they split. Marconius did what vampires do best when confronted with competition XD. The reason no one noticed is because the Kiasyd are such a small bloodline. Hardly anyone noticed when the Giovanni did their thing, and the Cappadocians were actually a large and legit clan.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, The Gentlemen Gamer wrote the Lore of the Bloodlines Kiasyd and he agrees that &quot;yes, Marconius is an asshat.&quot; So take that for what it's worth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T05:28:29-07:00","id":863115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mistress of whispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863113#post863113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wrote both the DA and BH Kiasyd, so I'd like to chime in here. Keep in mind that until/if it appears in the books, this is **all my headcanon**.<br /> <br /> My idea for the DA Kiasyd was prompted by all the mysteries and conflicting stories surrounding the modern Kiasyd, as well as the idea that fae/changelings were more prevalent pre-enlightenment. So I broadened the Kiasyd concept from Marconius and his 7-foot tall blue peeps, to all fae-touched vampires. The DA book didn't offer glimpses into the future so there was no way to outright connect them to the V20 Kiasyd, but I did leave some bread crumbs (like Marconius' claim that he was once a Lasombra and re-created himself through sorcery).<br /> <br /> Fast-forward to the BH book, where David and I felt the &quot;Maeghar&quot; would fit in perfectly. They're fae-touched, have seemingly suffered overwhelming loss (which makes them a great for the TMR) and are cloaked in secrecy (ditto). They also have a &quot;stay away from Marconius&quot; attitude.<br /> <br /> Given what we know about vampires in general (ruthless, broke no competition) and Lasombra-if-Marconius-was-one in particular (complete asshats), we probably know &quot;why&quot; they split. Marconius did what vampires do best when confronted with competition XD. The reason no one noticed is because the Kiasyd are such a small bloodline. Hardly anyone noticed when the Giovanni did their thing, and the Cappadocians were actually a large and legit clan.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, The Gentlemen Gamer wrote the Lore of the Bloodlines Kiasyd and he agrees that &quot;yes, Marconius is an asshat.&quot; So take that for what it's worth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's not to imply asshats can't be dangerous. This one stared into the Abyss for ooh... a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:07:51-07:00","id":863178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863074#post863074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for saying so. I'm a firm believer that bloodlines offer exciting diversity to those who want it. If the stereotype doesn't fit a chronicle, then don't play it, or play a character from the bloodline who isn't defined by his bloodline - it's as simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...I'll trust your good jugement (not that I have a choice). I just fear that Bloodlines would turn VtM into Pokemon, with scenarios like:<br /> <br /> After skin-head, shovel-head get Garbage-head, the new Bloodline with the weakness of having a Garbage-Face<br /> With their unique Discipline &quot;Smell of the dumpster&quot;:<br /> lvl 4 &quot;