ot sure how you'd rather I acted, but I've not actually taken issue with anything you've said.<br /> <br /> I'm not being sarcastic either. I don't think any of the bloodlines are as bad as you're making out. It's all opinion though, and you're welcome to yours <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:34:28-07:00","id":863267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863248#post863248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeez, I can only imagine how different your gracious responses are from the initial reactions after reading some of the unwarranted snark from a couple of posters in this thread! It's eye-twitch inducing. Kudos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slow down cowboy, I've provided two direct quotes from the corebook where Harbingers are called out as being made entirely out of massively powerful elders. Once as a rumor about the bloodline, and once as an out of character voice in the Background section. Saying that they totally have young members <i>is a retcon</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:37:05-07:00","id":863268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863261#post863261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not being sarcastic either. I don't think any of the bloodlines are as bad as you're making out. It's all opinion though, and you're welcome to yours <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hate opinions, it's futile and unproductive.<br /> I like art, and on the &quot;art&quot; level of things, you guys can do much better than this (it's not an opinion, it's a FACT).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:39:13-07:00","id":863270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=862755#post862755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Elder: </b>Harbingers of Skulls as a bloodline are dominated by elders, it's true, but the True Black Hand book states they've been newly Embracing due to their acknowledgement of being out-of-touch with the world today. <b>You don't have to play an elder Harbinger if you want to play one of their modern childer.</b> It's left nebulous when they began Embracing, so I'd give leeway of up to 40 years prior to today, off the top of my head. Again, you're going off of the core book, so you can still play a Harbinger - they were Embraced very shortly prior to their enforced 500 year &quot;torpor.&quot; When they wake in the modern nights they're still fledglings.<br /> <br /> <br /> If a player wanted me to describe what the Harbingers have that no other Clan possesses, <b>I would say they're a group of vampires who lost time</b>. No other Clan has &quot;history&quot; as an intrinsic stereotype. They weren't around to witness 500+ years of technological and cultural development, forcing them in these nights to quickly adapt or die. I could well see a Harbinger exposing himself to as much media as possible in an effort to remain relevant. A band of vampires childlike in their naivete about the modern world is a lot of fun to my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you see the contradiction here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:51:39-07:00","id":863274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863268#post863268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate opinions, it's futile and unproductive.<br /> I like art, and on the &amp;quot;art&amp;quot; level of things, you guys can do much better than this (it's not an opinion, it's a FACT).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a pity for you I guess. Hopefully future releases will have more artistic merit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:53:33-07:00","id":863275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863270#post863270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you see the contradiction here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the least, good sir. I presented options in that post. I decided to use the &quot;vampires who lost time&quot; as the way I'd present Harbingers to someone new. If someone wanted a deeper range, then I'd do as I've done with you and present multiple options. Everyone's a winner <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:59:46-07:00","id":863280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863268#post863268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate opinions, it's futile and unproductive.<br /> I like art, and on the &quot;art&quot; level of things, you guys can do much better than this (it's not an opinion, it's a FACT).</div> </div> </div> </div>How can anything regarding art be a fact. Beauty lies in the eye of the beholder, so the verdict whether something is on high or low level artistically is per definition an opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:08:27-07:00","id":863283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863280#post863280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How can anything regarding art be a fact. Beauty lies in the eye of the beholder, so the verdict whether something is on high or low level artistically is per definition an opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>okay, then, remove everything except the part &quot;you guys can do better than this&quot;...you disagree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:18:37-07:00","id":863286,"title":"","content":"I think that still counts as an opinion, I'm afraid. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't have nearly enough coffee in my system to think about Kindred pokemon with anything other than non-stop giggling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:19:44-07:00","id":863287,"title":"","content":"Thanks to the Wonders of Rolling Metaplot, things in the setting can change. So V20 published the Harbingers and says they're 100% dusty, re-animated elders. But then, Guide to the TMR comes out and <i>poof</i>, now they're creating Neonates to tackle the challenges of the modern world. This isn't a retcon. Its a <i>progression</i>. As in, V20 was correct for time values equal to or before X, but after time value X, GttTMR is now true.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of Rolling Metaplot, but it is how WW/OP operate. New books are considered to supplant older books because the new books happen &quot;later&quot; in &quot;time&quot; as far as the setting is concerned. <br /> <br /> Now if they'd just get over their unwillingness to ignore past material in the name of internal logical consistency... that'd be something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:30:25-07:00","id":863295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863287#post863287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks to the Wonders of Rolling Metaplot, things in the setting can change. So V20 published the Harbingers and says they're 100% dusty, re-animated elders. But then, Guide to the TMR comes out and <i>poof</i>, now they're creating Neonates to tackle the challenges of the modern world. This isn't a retcon. Its a <i>progression</i>. As in, V20 was correct for time values equal to or before X, but after time value X, GttTMR is now true.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of Rolling Metaplot, but it is how WW/OP operate. New books are considered to supplant older books because the new books happen &quot;later&quot; in &quot;time&quot; as far as the setting is concerned.<br /> <br /> Now if they'd just get over their unwillingness to ignore past material in the name of internal logical consistency... that'd be something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well put. I'd add that even if V20 typifies Harbingers as dusty elders, there's never been a prohibition on the bloodline Embracing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:45:49-07:00","id":863303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863295#post863295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well put. I'd add that even if V20 typifies Harbingers as dusty elders, there's never been a prohibition on the bloodline Embracing.</div> </div> </div> </div>All this talk about Harbingers has made me think... imagine a Neonate arrived to the Feast of Folly, was buried undead in Kaymakli and then managed to last for centuries and become a Harbinger, having spent most of the centuries in torpor.<br /> <br /> Would she be an Elder with the traits of a Neonate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:48:49-07:00","id":863307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863303#post863303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All this talk about Harbingers has made me think... imagine a Neonate arrived to the Feast of Folly, was buried undead in Kaymakli and then managed to last for centuries and become a Harbinger, having spent most of the centuries in torpor.<br /> <br /> Would she be an Elder with the traits of a Neonate?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would depend on whether the vampire succumbed to torpor or not. Technically a neonate Harbinger could survive in the Shadowlands, albeit with a great deal of difficulty. As I mentioned before - the right combination of Allies, Contacts, Mentor, and the like would help support a weaker vampire trapped in the Shadowlands. Also bear in mind that after the entombment in Kaymakli, many Cappadocians likely committed diablerie on one another as blood drew low. You may only be a vampire of 30 years, but if you've somehow consumed several elders, you might stand a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:50:05-07:00","id":863310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863303#post863303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would she be an Elder with the traits of a Neonate?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the blood gets more potent during Torpor, It would be an elder with Ancillae traits. Although, I doubt she would act as your common elder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T14:09:17-07:00","id":863323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863268#post863268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate opinions, it's futile and unproductive.<br /> I like art, and on the &quot;art&quot; level of things, you guys can do much better than this (it's not an opinion, it's a FACT).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's...not what &quot;fact&quot; means, amigo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T14:17:10-07:00","id":863327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863307#post863307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would depend on whether the vampire succumbed to torpor or not. Technically a neonate Harbinger could survive in the Shadowlands, albeit with a great deal of difficulty. As I mentioned before - the right combination of Allies, Contacts, Mentor, and the like would help support a weaker vampire trapped in the Shadowlands. Also bear in mind that after the entombment in Kaymakli, many Cappadocians likely committed diablerie on one another as blood drew low. You may only be a vampire of 30 years, but if you've somehow consumed several elders, you might stand a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it still an open question as to how exactly the harbingers survived? Do PC harbingers get anything that would allow them to replicate the feat? Because eating ghosts is not something Cappadocians were ever capable of. Fiddling with the Underworld was a Giovanni and Nagaraja thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T14:20:58-07:00","id":863328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863327#post863327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it still an open question as to how exactly the harbingers survived? Do PC harbingers get anything that would allow them to replicate the feat? Because eating ghosts is not something Cappadocians were ever capable of. Fiddling with the Underworld was a Giovanni and Nagaraja thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do indeed. There's a ritual provided in the book for all your Shadowlands feeding needs. You should buy a copy and let us know what you think! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:21:28-07:00","id":863347,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear that. Way back when the Harbingers were first introduced I remember scratching my head at some text referring to them surviving on the only vitae available in the Underworld: that of their fellows. Yeah, that would maybe work for a few weeks or months depending on how many Cappadocians originally made it across the Shroud, but it sure wouldn't have tided them over for centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T17:44:20-07:00","id":863402,"title":"","content":"So caveat beforehand: I've not read this book yet. <br /> <br /> So something I'm kinda worried about here in regards to Bloodline write ups.<br /> <br /> From what people have posted here there is a sorta explanation for why the Kiasyd in Dark Ages V20 were different from any version we have seen before. Seems there has been a lot of really good conversation between different writers in regards to it. So now the V20DA one fits into the setting a little better and provides an extra option for players in V20 too if they want. That's kinda awesome.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind I was wondering about some other bloodlines and there various write ups across the V20 line. <br /> <br /> <b>Lamia:</b> We get the basic version of these guys in V20 in a couple of paragraphs. They get a bit of a reinterpretation in V20DA and a sidebar suggesting that they eventually cut a deal with the Giovanni and go into hiding (possibly in the Underworld) until the final nights. From the posts here its suggested that the Harbingers kinda created a bloodline that is the &quot;Lamia Reborn&quot; basically. <br /> <br /> So this has me scratching my head a little. Particularly because said &quot;new version&quot; does not get a full right up. Obviously a ST could use the either option of &quot;hidden survivors&quot; or &quot;new creations&quot; but I was wondering how easy it might be to reconcile the two groups if you wanted to do that? Also does this book detail a new version of the Twilight Garden Necromancy path first introduced in V20DA?<br /> <br /> <b>True Brujah:</b> Once again they get a pretty minimal summary in V20 and an expansion (and slight thematic update) in V20DA. From comments here it seems they don't get a full write up (which honestly I don't mind, as while they do need more fluff, we have a chapter on them coming up in Lore of the Bloodlines), but I guess some new info it included right? Did any of the writers on this book also do their upcoming write up in Lore of the Bloodlines? Is it the same writer as the one that did their write up in V20DA? I wonder because this bloodline has actually been pretty consistent in the fluff since their inception and I'm hoping they stay that way. <br /> <br /> <b>Old Clan Tzimisce:</b> So basic idea of a few paragraphs in V20. Couple more paragraphs in V20DA. General theme of &quot;No Vicissitude&quot; has been constant in them, along with a &quot;dark reserved nobility&quot;. Soul Eater and confusing contradictory clan fluff has slowly been getting stripped off them since Revised. From comments and reviews I read this book seems to basically bring that to a close. Likewise, from comments it seems this book explains how they got rid of the Vicissitude attribute in their blood and why they practice Koldunism more then other Tzimisce. So all good stuff. Apparently this book also explains why Koldunism changed from a regional based magic to a more abstract elemental based magic between Dark Ages and Modern V20. All good stuff. <br /> <br /> My only question is the V20DA idea that they called themselves and were called &quot;The Dracul&quot; included? As I always thought it was weird they called themselves &quot;Old Clan&quot; rather then something like &quot;True&quot; or had an original name or something. Its a minor thing, but it would be nice for consistency. Also I know one of the new paths of Koldunism is a V20DA style one based around Enoch. What is the other one?<br /> <br /> <b>Harbingers of Skulls:</b> So these guys got same paragraph treatment as most Bloodlines in V20, and it was pretty much a straight rehash of their Revised edition fluff (though its nice to now there is now an explanation for how they survived in the Underworld without blood). Rites of Blood expanded on them a bit in the Sabbat chapter. Lore of the Clans has some interesting new hints about them from the Giovanni perspective. <br /> <br /> I'm curious as to how this new book meshes the idea they are members of the Black Hand with the old fluff of them being Sabbat members? Is it a case that some of the elders (the more revenge driven ones) went to the Sabbat while the more occultish ones went to the TBH? Also, who wrote up the Harbingers for this book? Are they the same writer as for Lore the Bloodlines? As honestly as a bloodline they have never had the largest word count, so new fluff is welcome but I'm hoping it can be presented as consistent new fluff.<br /> <br /> <b>Baali:</b> Oh god...these guys. Fluff consistency and them really don't get along. V20 has the &quot;Hail Satan!&quot; version in it. Rites of Blood has the &quot;Infernalists on Steroids&quot; (AKA the NEW BAALI of Azreal's mindset) version that fits with the old Dark Ages fluff pre-Clanbook Baali. V20DA too a careful view on them and basically said all their different backstories might be true to a certain degree (basically &quot;ST's pick your own Baali background&quot;). So which flavour do we get in this book? <br /> <br /> I've given up hoping for fluff consistency with this bloodline. I'm just curious which flavour we are getting more of (or even a new flavour) person I'd like more of the Cthulhu &quot;Children&quot; flavour, but meh. Likewise, I'm wondering if they share and writer in between V20DA (Neall I believe?), GttTMR (since I've heard info about them is scattered all over this book) and the upcoming Lore of the Bloodlines? Since at least three sources will then hopefully have some fluff consistency for them. <br /> <br /> Also do the Hand now fight them or support them? I remember Dirty Secrets really stressed the hate on that the Hand had for the Baali. So I was wondering if they are discussed as members or as possible enemies (or both!)?<br /> <br /> <b>Nagaraja:</b> OK, so these are the big one for me. I'm a massive fan of this bloodline. Despite the fact that they pretty much typify a lot of things I disliked about Masquerade. Special snowflake among special snowflakes (check), nearly unplayable (check), completely different characterization depending on writer (check), weird niche bloodline discipline (check). Still despite that I really adore them. <br /> <br /> So their fluff pre-V20 was pretty badly muddled (despite there not being a whole lot of it) and scattered across about three Vampire books and three Mage books. V20 did a pretty good job of reducing them down to their most basic concept and giving players a little more wiggle room with them. V20DA added to that with some updated and consolidated background that kept the skeleton of their awesome old fluff without overstuffing it with issues from Mage. So I'm pretty happy with how they are sitting at current in the V20 line. <br /> <br /> Does this book add new fluff to them? Does it manage to rework some of the weirder and clunkier stuff from their Dirty Secrets fluff in and make it work better? Does it do a good job of fitting in their Mage fluff ties without getting to &quot;into&quot; Mage fluff emphasis? Also was their write up in this book done by Neall like V20DA and is he the writer for their chapter in Lore of the Bloodlines? <br /> <br /> Also the Idran get a write up in this book apparently? How is that handled, as I thought the few members that were not hunted down by their fellow Chakrivanti ended up as the Nagaraja thanks to the botched ritual? Are they Litches? <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for anyone who takes the time to answer these questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T19:54:36-07:00","id":863450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863402#post863402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So caveat beforehand: I've not read this book yet.<br /> <br /> So something I'm kinda worried about here in regards to Bloodline write ups.<br /> <br /> From what people have posted here there is a sorta explanation for why the Kiasyd in Dark Ages V20 wer