or Suicides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T04:34:38-07:00","id":863567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863524#post863524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Props to you for the detailed query! However, my honest advice here has to be that you're best off reading the book. You're asking a lot of questions that are better covered by the content we've written. For my part, I will answer that I wrote the Harbingers for this, for Lore of the Bloodlines, and provided Cappadocians some fair coverage in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. Also, they are not exclusively in the Sabbat, even if several of their number rest within that Sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Mr Gamer for that reply. <br /> <br /> I appreciate that I many went overboard with the questions in my last post. Did not realise how much of a content spoil I was asking for until I re-read it today. Anyway thanks for the answer to the Harbinger writer question. Its nice to know the Onyx Path guys got the same writer for all these different sources of the Harbingers! Woo fluff consistency! <br /> <br /> I really hope that they got Neall back for the Nagaraja on this book and Lore of the Bloodlines. I felt he did a really good job with them in V20DA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T06:24:05-07:00","id":863589,"title":"","content":"So I just read the book and I don't like it as a whole. The Tal'Mahe'Ra always stroke me as a kind of odd in the world of darkness and I prefer to see the sect dissolved (or never formed) and all the fingers being split between different factions without links with each other.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said aside, it's a great book. The introduced mechanics are fun, and I can see myself using most of them. Just not in the intended way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T06:29:11-07:00","id":863594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863567#post863567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Mr Gamer for that reply.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that I many went overboard with the questions in my last post. Did not realise how much of a content spoil I was asking for until I re-read it today. Anyway thanks for the answer to the Harbinger writer question. Its nice to know the Onyx Path guys got the same writer for all these different sources of the Harbingers! Woo fluff consistency!<br /> <br /> I really hope that they got Neall back for the Nagaraja on this book and Lore of the Bloodlines. I felt he did a really good job with them in V20DA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the compliment, but other writers did Nagaraja in this book and in Lore of the Bloodlines. I think they both did great jobs!<br /> <br /> I wrote on Lore of the Bloodlines, though. I did Enoch in TMR20 and Salubri in LotB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T06:45:45-07:00","id":863602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863310#post863310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the blood gets more potent during Torpor, It would be an elder with Ancillae traits. Although, I doubt she would act as your common elder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're getting at here precisely. How exactly does blood become more potent in torpor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:04:17-07:00","id":863610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863602#post863602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you're getting at here precisely. How exactly does blood become more potent in torpor?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant, Disciplines and Attributes increase during Torpor, but they can't go over the generation limit (with perhaps rare exceptions).<br /> The process is slow. but for a torpid 6th gen, for exemple, going from dot 6 to dot 7 is a huge step, even if it got him 100 years of torpor.<br /> <br /> There are no precise mechanics for it, try Children of the Night for reference.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:45:11-07:00","id":863638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863589#post863589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I just read the book and I don't like it as a whole. The Tal'Mahe'Ra always stroke me as a kind of odd in the world of darkness and I prefer to see the sect dissolved (or never formed) and all the fingers being split between different factions without links with each other.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said aside, it's a great book. The introduced mechanics are fun, and I can see myself using most of them. Just not in the intended way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be sure to leave a review on DTRPG! Your feedback is much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:30:35-07:00","id":863711,"title":"","content":"For anyone on the writing team who might know, are there any future plans for the reimagined mummies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T10:04:10-07:00","id":863737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863594#post863594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the compliment, but other writers did Nagaraja in this book and in Lore of the Bloodlines. I think they both did great jobs!<br /> <br /> I wrote on Lore of the Bloodlines, though. I did Enoch in TMR20 and Salubri in LotB.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thanks so much for the reply Neall, much appreciated. <br /> <br /> I'll take it on faith if you like the write ups for the Nagaraja in TMR20 and LotB that they are good and fit with what's already been written by previous authors. <br /> <br /> Your doing the Salubri chapter, thats awesome. I really liked the Presence inclusion on the Healers discipline list. So I'm interested to see what other new stuff you've got in store for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:56:38-07:00","id":863806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863594#post863594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the compliment, but other writers did Nagaraja in this book and in Lore of the Bloodlines. I think they both did great jobs!<br /> <br /> I wrote on Lore of the Bloodlines, though. I did Enoch in TMR20 and Salubri in LotB.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, you did Salubri in DAV20 as well? I liked what was done with them there.<br /> <br /> If I may, could you expand on what you imagined when you described the Doomsday Clock, since you wrote Enoch in TMR20? I didn't quite get if the ghosts were meant to be like kites at the end of the chains kept afloat at sky level by the winds, if they are in the water, or across between the spires and the walls.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:18:59-07:00","id":863815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861343#post861343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are 6 instances of the word 'Drakaina' in the book.<br /> pg. 49: In the sidebox about playable bloodlines</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=861343#post861343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are we supposed to just assume they are identical to Dark Ages' Lamiae, but without the Cappadocians around? Is that it?<br /> They are not explained in the Bloodlines section, nothing?<br /> If that's the case, I find it extremely... irritating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a deliberate omission? I'm reading chapter 2 now (&quot;Bahari \u2014 Cult of the Dark Mother&quot;) and the Drakaina sound interesting. I can extrapolate a little based on the few passages, but I'd love to know what the developers had in mind. Will supplementary material about this bloodline be made available anywhere?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:25:52-07:00","id":863822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you for Sophia-Amunet. My beloved mummies! </div> </div> </div>You're entirely welcome. ^_^ I admit, Sophia-Amunet is what happens when I'm smitten with 'HE is a dryly snarky Baali Methuselah, SHE is an ickle Amenti tykebomb/person of mass destruction, together they HUNT INFERNALISTS' in the middle of the night and my brain just runs with it from there. <hr />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wyrd Sister<br /> Freelance Penmonkey For Hire<br /> Moloch's PR Chick</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3896-nagaina","name":"Nagaina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:37:31-07:00","id":863871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863638#post863638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be sure to leave a review on DTRPG! Your feedback is much appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will as soon as I finish reading the book. But so far I'm loving it, even if the structure is a bit chaotic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T14:47:57-07:00","id":863911,"title":"","content":"I think I might get this book soon. I was always a fan of the original Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand (I know I'm in the minority on that one, though) and I look forward to seeing how V20 handles the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T17:30:39-07:00","id":863984,"title":"","content":"My review on DriveThruRPG goes along these same lines, but know that I believe this is FAR from being a perfect book\u2026<br /> <br /> First of all, the various chapters do not build upon one another in any linear way. Rather, they interlock in ways that don\u2019t make sense until you\u2019ve read it all \u2013 and even then it\u2019s sometimes hard to find the proper connexions. That is, mentions in Chapter One of groups or ideas don\u2019t come up \u2018in the spotlight\u2019 until Chapter Four, and things show up in Chapter Three that demand going back to read Chapter Two. This is, I feel, less a problem than a FEATURE of the subject matter. The Black Hand is, by its very nature, a tangled web of knots, and I\u2019m going to be coming back to this book over and over to figure out how to unravel the Hand\u2019s motives and activities.<br /> <br /> Second, there ARE holes in the text. Drakaina, revenants, blood magics, and the place of Enoch\u2019s waterfront district on the Sea of Shadows, these all are dead ends in the book. The thing is, what would a book about the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra BE without those? Sure, <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</i> had more blocked streets than thoroughfares (or so we all seem to remember), but THIS book\u2019s dangling bits more often come in the flavour of evocative rather than malicious omissions. Of course, I WOULD like to have the promised Appendix with \u2013 if possible \u2013 ghoul families and a modern take on the Danava, but that\u2019s not a deal breaker for me.<br /> <br /> Third, it does contradict itself in subtle and gross ways, and THAT, my friends, is what the <i>Manus Nigrum</i> has ever been all about!<br /> <br /> Finally, I gotta say that yeah, I kinda love the book! It\u2019s lit fires in my mind that hadn\u2019t been there before, and I call that a win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T21:52:57-07:00","id":864117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=863815#post863815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a deliberate omission? I'm reading chapter 2 now (&quot;Bahari \u2014 Cult of the Dark Mother&quot;) and the Drakaina sound interesting. I can extrapolate a little based on the few passages, but I'd love to know what the developers had in mind. Will supplementary material about this bloodline be made available anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Material was cut. Some discussion is ongoing. Can't say much more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T23:35:54-07:00","id":864147,"title":"","content":"I would be very happy if information on the Drakaina and the BLack Hand's Revenant families could be put back in to the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1456-zeke-hubris","name":"Zeke Hubris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T23:37:38-07:00","id":864148,"title":"","content":"I do miss the revenant families.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T00:42:56-07:00","id":864164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeke Hubris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864147#post864147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be very happy if information on the Drakaina and the BLack Hand's Revenant families could be put back in to the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Drakaina should be included in the book. However, I would be happy if the families of the Black Hand were taken into V20 Ghouls. That way, all the information on Ghouls and all the revenant families would be in a single book, instead of scattered around a dozen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T00:45:01-07:00","id":864165,"title":"","content":"I do agree that a small writeup of the Drakaina should be in The Black Hand and that the revenant families should get a writeup in V20 Ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:05:05-07:00","id":864214,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> Can somebody tell me how Vicissitude and the Soul Eater thing was solved in this book? I contemplate buying it, but I worry of getting another book of self-censored that DS 1 was. I consider the first Dirty Secrets a warning to all writers why you should not drink more than a glas of wine before writing stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:41:08-07:00","id":864230,"title":"","content":"It is very strange that the Soul Eater review is being rarely discussed that topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:14:58-07:00","id":864251,"title":"","content":"I caved and got it. I really like it this far, and that's high praise from someone who doesn't usually like Vampire :P<br /> <br /> Also, Vampires still coma back as Wraiths according to the book, so much about that rumor <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T07:21:29-07:00","id":864277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864214#post864214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!Can somebody tell me how Vicissitude and the Soul Eater thing was solved in this book? I contemplate buying it, but I worry of getting another book of self-censored that DS 1 was. I consider the first Dirty Secrets a warning to all writers why you should not drink more than a glas of wine before writing stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Soul Eater thing was replaced with Asakku. It is explicitly called out that Asakku's reality is optional, and that it may be self-delusion on the part of its Kindred investigators that perhaps others have taken advantage of.<br /> <br /> So what is Asakku? A small group in the Black Hand has noticed that when some vampires study Vicissitude, <i>something</i> makes contact with them, offering them power in return for the ability to manifest itself. If they accept, they lose their identities to it, becoming its vessels.<br /> <br /> The two most prominent theories the group has are that either it's a form of madness, the vampire coming to identify with the Discipline to the extent their original consciousness is obliterated, or... it's a manifestation of the Watchers, the Second Generation, seeking to return to the physical world. Misapprehension about the first time the group discovered Asakku resulted in the Soul Eater idea popping up - that is, the belief Vicissitude was contracted from a spirit, etc. - but this is explicitly <i>not</i> the case, as it's established the Tzimisce Ante had Vicissitude from the earliest times.<br /> <br /> (If you know your WoD cosmology, reading about the first case of Asakku might get you wondering about connections to the Neverborn Malfeans instead...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:23:15-07:00","id":864305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864277#post864277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Soul Eater thing was replaced with Asakku. It is explicitly called out that Asakku's reality is optional, and that it may be self-delusion on the part of its Kindred investigators that perhaps others have taken advantage of.<br /> <br /> So what is Asakku? A small group in the Black Hand has noticed that when some vampires study Vicissitude, <i>something</i> makes contact with them, offering them power in return for the ability to manifest itself. If they accept, they lose their identities to it, becoming its vessels.<br /> <br /> The two most prominent theories the group has are that either it's a form of madness, the vampire coming to identify with the Discipline to the extent their original consciousness is obliterated, or... it's a manifestation of the Watchers, the Second Generation, seeking to return to the physical world. Misapprehension about the first time the group discovered Asakku resulted in the Soul Eater idea popping up - that is, the belief Vicissitude was contracted from a spirit, etc. - but this is explicitly <i>not</i> the case, as it's established the Tzimisce Ante had Vicissitude from the earliest times.<br /> <br /> (If you know your WoD cosmology, reading about the first case of Asakku might get you wondering about connections to the Neverborn Malfeans instead...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Especially since Vicissitude would seemingly have nothing to do with Malfeans. Which makes me wonder . . . is it actually being a part of the TMR that turns people to Asakku instead? As in, it's proximity to the Malfeans (dwelling Enoch) that is the real culprit, and not Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> Yes, I've probably added 2+2 and got pi squared, but what's a ludicrous, unsupported fan theory among friends?<br /> <br /> I'm definitely buying this book. I just can't wait for it to arrive in print!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-12-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:30:07-07:00","id":864311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864277#post864277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Soul Eater thing was replaced with Asakku. It is explicitly called out that Asakku's reality is optional, and that it may be self-delusion on the part of its Kindred investigators that perhaps others have taken advantage of.<br /> <br /> So what is Asakku? A small group in the Black Hand has noticed that when some vampires study Vicissitude, <i>something</i> makes contact with them, offering them power in return for the ability to manifest itself. If they accept, they lose their identities to it, becoming its vessels.<br /> <br /> The two most prominent theories the group has are that either it's a form of madness, the vampire coming to identify with the Discipline to the extent their original consciousness is obliterated, or... it's a manifestation of the Watchers, the Second Generation, seeking to return to the physical world. Misapprehension about the first time the group discovered Asakku resulted in the Soul Eater idea popping up - that is, the belief Vicissitude was contracted from a spirit, etc. - but this is explicitly <i>not</i> the case, as it's established the Tzimisce Ante had Vicissitude from the earliest times.<br /> <br /> (If you know your WoD cosmology, reading about the first case of Asakku might get you wondering about connections to the Neverborn Malfeans instead...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I never asked for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:38:18-07:00","id":864320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864311#post864311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never asked for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me, I've rechecked the book 3 times...<i><b>Revised</b></i> is salvation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 04-12-2016, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:51:21-07:00","id":864392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864320#post864320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trust me, I've rechecked the book 3 times...<i><b>Revised</b></i> is salvation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> Hardly, 80% of Revised background are part of the problem VtM got over time. It was the try by the writers to force one style of play on the player community. &quot;Tonnenideologie&quot; it would be called here. I am quite pleased with how V20 turned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T11:32:02-07:00","id":864410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcL</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading chapter 2 now (&quot;Bahari \u2014 Cult of the Dark Mother&quot;) and the Drakaina sound interesting. I can extrapolate a little based on the few passages, but I'd love to know what the developers had in mind. Will supplementary material about this bloodline be made available anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864117#post864117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Material was cut. Some discussion is ongoing. Can't say much more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The material on the Drakaina felt truncated. Thanks for the confirmation. I think they're sketched out well enough in the book for GMs to fill in the blanks if they need to, but I'm looking forward to seeing them get a longer writeup somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T11:59:05-07:00","id":864415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864392#post864392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Tonnenideologie&quot; it would be called here. I am quite pleased with how V20 turned out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't around long enough to know about that. But I agree that V20 sandbox can offer more to &quot;creative&quot; writers/players...which I'm not.<br /> It's true that part of my dislike for v20 (and requiem) is the open playstyle that is inconvenient for me. But that's not all.<br /> <br /> What trully bothers me is the lack of depth.<br /> <br /> So you make a new path with its followers having Vicissitude which is all about using vicissitude and converting its users. okay...that's it?<br /> So Anarchs get blood powers to hack internet and spoil the camarilla...that's it?<br /> <br /> How am I supposed to get new ideas this way? I could've done the same (despite my lack of imagination).<br /> <br /> I need something more than just shallow descriptions, pokemon powers and patchwork bloodlines.<br /> I need ideas, deep, complex constructed ideas...something I wouldn't have thought about. Something that would force me to think and re-think for hours, days until I can decide if and how I can use it best or simply use it as proposed.<br /> <br /> The authors call it &quot;expanding&quot;, I call it &quot;stretching&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 04-12-2016, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:06:05-07:00","id":864421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864410#post864410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The material on the Drakaina felt truncated. Thanks for the confirmation. I think they're sketched out well enough in the book for GMs to fill in the blanks if they need to, but I'm looking forward to seeing them get a longer writeup somewhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's just that it they don't get a writeup in the Guide of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, the Rites of Blood or the Lore of the Bloodlines, I don't really get where we're gonna find them. It's not like the dev could push a tiny hidden bloodline of necromancers belonging to a mysterious sect in any book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:35:49-07:00","id":864437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864277#post864277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (If you know your WoD cosmology, reading about the first case of Asakku might get you wondering about connections to the Neverborn Malfeans instead...)</div> </div> </div> </div>...Abyssal Exalted shout-out time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:37:04-07:00","id":864438,"title":"","content":"@everyone who wants a Drakaina write-up: that would be nice, but I don't get from where you reached the conclusion they are a bloodline. They are a group of Bahari Harbingers who Embraced some witches and venerate Lilith in a cult inspired by the Lamia. <br /> <br /> That's the only thing I get from the passage &quot;Three mortal witches submitted to the Lazarene Harbingers\u2019 Embrace and revived Lamia\u2019s order as the Drakaina.&quot;, and actually it doesn't seem to need much more, since the Drakaina are basically some Harbingers Bahari, and we get write-ups for both Harbingers and Bahari in the book.<br /> <br /> Now, I might be wrong and the Drakaina may be a distinct bloodline, and it would be nice to have them detailed somewhere if it is the case. Lore of the Bloodlines, for instance, would be a good place to have either a Drakaina bloodline write-up or a Drakaina-as-a-group expanded description, under the Harbingers section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:37:06-07:00","id":864439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864415#post864415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't around long enough to know about that. But I agree that V20 sandbox can offer more to &quot;creative&quot; writers/players...which I'm not.<br /> I need something more than just shallow descriptions, pokemon powers and patchwork bloodlines.<br /> I need ideas, deep, complex constructed ideas...something I wouldn't have thought about. Something that would force me to think and re-think for hours, days until I can decide if and how I can use it best or simply use it as proposed.<br /> <br /> The authors call it &quot;expanding&quot;, I call it &quot;stretching&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> I see your point and why the sandbox starting approach of V20 can be problematic for players who consider themselves &quot;less creative&quot;. Which I find dubious, because if you go the RPG way, you have to have some creativity, otherwise you would not be playing rpgs.<br /> Sandbox and Depth of background stuff are mostly exclusive, since to give the Sandbox players their room, you cannot go too deep into the matters. This is good for players like me and my group, since we can finetune what we have without problems and build on this with our own stuff and playstyle. I see why that can be chaffing for players who like an extremly deep background world to start with, especially if they have not much time to prepare games.Here in Germany, the rpg &quot;DSA&quot; is one with an extremly developed background, but while that is a great thing if you had few time to prepare a gaming evening, it can become a burden too. I only came back to DSA with the new edition, since they lightened some things.<br /> <br /> But back to VtM: I recognise the appeal Revised has for players like you. It went deep into the various areas of play (and I have to say that some stuff dealing with the periphery like Havens of the Damned was good) and it could have been a great version of VtM if not for the fact that Revised screwed over a lot of the canon of 1st/2ed. The writers back then tried to press all players to play in the style &quot;personal horror&quot; to the exclusion of all else. &quot;Blood treachery&quot; is one example where they went overboard ruleswise to make sure that only their own interpretation was playable.<br /> But the crowing of this was how the writers reintrepreted the various Clans and Bloodlines. Several became unplayable and more the changed fluff made the survival of those clans and Bloodlines illogical, since so much infighting and strife would have meant that many Clans would have fallen and never reached the Now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:10:36-07:00","id":864476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864438#post864438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@everyone who wants a Drakaina write-up: that would be nice, but I don't get from where you reached the conclusion they are a bloodline. They are a group of Bahari Harbingers who Embraced some witches and venerate Lilith in a cult inspired by the Lamia.<br /> <br /> That's the only thing I get from the passage &quot;Three mortal witches submitted to the Lazarene Harbingers\u2019 Embrace and revived Lamia\u2019s order as the Drakaina.&quot;, and actually it doesn't seem to need much more, since the Drakaina are basically some Harbingers Bahari, and we get write-ups for both Harbingers and Bahari in the book.<br /> <br /> Now, I might be wrong and the Drakaina may be a distinct bloodline, and it would be nice to have them detailed somewhere if it is the case. Lore of the Bloodlines, for instance, would be a good place to have either a Drakaina bloodline write-up or a Drakaina-as-a-group expanded description, under the Harbingers section.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 49, just in the section called Bloodlines of the Hand at the Information Age entry. It's clearly stated that the Drakaina are a bloodline distinct from the Harbingers who just happens to be listed after them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:10:36-07:00","id":864516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864438#post864438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the only thing I get from the passage &quot;Three mortal witches submitted to the Lazarene Harbingers\u2019 Embrace and revived Lamia\u2019s order as the Drakaina.&quot;, and actually it doesn't seem to need much more, since the Drakaina are basically some Harbingers Bahari, and we get write-ups for both Harbingers and Bahari in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was exactly my take on it as well. I don't think the Drakaina are a &quot;bloodline&quot; in any meaningful sense of the word. I was asking mostly because I've always liked both the Cappadocian/Harbingers storyline and the Lilin/Bahari, so I sensed a chocolate &amp; peanut butter situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:04:40-07:00","id":864554,"title":"","content":"VtM is <b><i>not</i></b> &quot;Sandbox&quot; at all. It has an intricate setting, a huge metaplot and they even incorporate mechanical rules changes into their metaplot. There's nothing customizable, modular or sandboxy about VtM material at all. In fact, it's *extremely* defined and pre-set. You're not using their tools to build your own world, you're playing in <i>their</i> world. VtM campaigns are basically fanfiction for the metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:19:21-07:00","id":864565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864554#post864554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM is <b><i>not</i></b> &amp;quot;Sandbox&amp;quot; at all. It has an intricate setting, a huge metaplot and they even incorporate mechanical rules changes into their metaplot. There's nothing customizable, modular or sandboxy about VtM material at all. In fact, it's *extremely* defined and pre-set. You're not using their tools to build your own world, you're playing in <i>their</i> world. VtM campaigns are basically fanfiction for the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know man I've ran my own sand box games and no one from white wolf kicked my door down and hauled me off to metaplot reeducation camp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:30:02-07:00","id":864575,"title":"","content":"The game is not *designed* for that. You can use a knife to eat yogurt, too, it's just not the intended use of a knife. There <i>are</i> sandbox games. That's a term that has specific meaning in RPG design. There are games like Savage Worlds that can be adapted to any plot, any setting, whatever. They're sandbox games. You're given tools to build whatever you want, like LEGOs. VtM is not LEGOs. And if VtM was LEGOs, it would be one of the &quot;built this thing from that movie&quot; kits. Not the big box of bricks to enjoy with nothing but your imagination and physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T16:26:25-07:00","id":864601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864575#post864575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game is not *designed* for that. You can use a knife to eat yogurt, too, it's just not the intended use of a knife. There <i>are</i> sandbox games. That's a term that has specific meaning in RPG design. There are games like Savage Worlds that can be adapted to any plot, any setting, whatever. They're sandbox games. You're given tools to build whatever you want, like LEGOs. VtM is not LEGOs. And if VtM was LEGOs, it would be one of the &quot;built this thing from that movie&quot; kits. Not the big box of bricks to enjoy with nothing but your imagination and physics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, what you are calling a Sandbox game is a universal game. or Toolbox game. Sandbox style gaming is built on Player proactiveness. If you have a plot with plans and features its not a sandbox game. If &quot;Ok the players do stuff the world reacts, or goes on itsown&quot; that's sandbox.<br /> <br /> Arguably I'd say V:TM is less one coherent canon and more 3 or 4 related things that you have to hammer together to get a whole and it will still look abit funny(kind of like trying to get a &quot;One world of Darkness!&quot;). There are some intrinsic truisms(Vampires drink blood, Vampires don't sparkle etc) but there is a decent amount of both ambiguity and different books definately define different styles of play and almost separate worlds for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T17:43:00-07:00","id":864631,"title":"","content":"Being not as up on my Wraith lore as I perhaps should be, the book did get me thinking, &quot;Do wraiths have any defense against necromancy other than 'kill Necromancer immediately'?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T18:50:06-07:00","id":864664,"title":"","content":"Not really, no. Wraiths don't have much defense against the living, except for their Arcanoi.. which aren't good at beating up the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T21:18:33-07:00","id":864697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864664#post864664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, no. Wraiths don't have much defense against the living, except for their Arcanoi.. which aren't good at beating up the living.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were pitting wraith PCs against vampire NPCs, I'd probably allow a Willpower roll to defend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T22:34:36-07:00","id":864717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864554#post864554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM is <b><i>not</i></b> &quot;Sandbox&quot; at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about <b>V20</b> (not the corebook, the other books), there's not enough stuff in them to call metaplot. that's why I go <b>Revised</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864697#post864697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were pitting wraith PCs against vampire NPCs, I'd probably allow a Willpower roll to defend.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make things hell easier for non-Necromancers, no? (Don't know much about Wraiths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 04-13-2016, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T23:15:55-07:00","id":864729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864575#post864575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game is not *designed* for that. You can use a knife to eat yogurt, too, it's just not the intended use of a knife. There <i>are</i> sandbox games. That's a term that has specific meaning in RPG design. There are games like Savage Worlds that can be adapted to any plot, any setting, whatever. They're sandbox games. You're given tools to build whatever you want, like LEGOs. VtM is not LEGOs. And if VtM was LEGOs, it would be one of the &quot;built this thing from that movie&quot; kits. Not the big box of bricks to enjoy with nothing but your imagination and physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're conflating sandbox/toolbox settings with sandbox-style games. Requiem is an explicitly toolbox setting. Masquerade was relatively open-ended in 1e and 2e, went through a few metaplot-driven years during Revised, and has swung around to a &quot;choose whatever option works for you&quot; format for V20. I'd say V20 is more &quot;choose your own adventure&quot; than pure toolbox, but I digress.<br /> <br /> Sandbox-style games can be run in conjunction with either type of setting. If I slavishly adhere to metaplot and turn a coterie of PCs loose in a 2001 New York City where the Camarilla just ousted the Sabbat and Calebros stepped down as Prince and Don Polonia still has a suntan problem, I'm running my game in a non-modular, out-of-the-box setting. If I have no overarching storyline planned beyond &quot;have the world react to PC actions,&quot; I'm running a sandbox game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T23:23:45-07:00","id":864733,"title":"","content":"I have two questions?<br /> <br /> Do is understand this correctly that the &quot;Cult&quot; Background cost two points per point (the test is not very clear written imo)? And can you purchase points in the included Backgrounds on top of it?<br /> (For example having personal Herd on top having a Cult?)<br /> <br /> Which roles are effected by the Berserker Merit? Ony Attack and Parry or also Damage and Soak rolls or even combat related discipline powers? (And isn't this Merit completely overpowered?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T02:09:38-07:00","id":864781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864554#post864554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM is <b><i>not</i></b> &quot;Sandbox&quot; at..</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> I think you confuse sandbox and toolbox. Toolbox systems like Savage Worlds, Fuzion, Cyphersystem, D&amp;D 3+, Genre Division, etc. give a rules framework and then you can do anything you like with it. Many of these toolbox systems have one or two main designermade settings (e.g. Numenera for Cypher), which are sandboxes to play with.<br /> A sandbox system has a rules set and a broad setting, but the setting is openended for the gaming groups to fill in. VtM is definitely a sandbox system since there is a fixed background, but how you play it out is your groups choice. There is no OPP police coming for you if you decide to play a group of Gangrel in the hinterland woods and what they do for 400 years, instead of a city campaign with intense politics and most clans involved.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T04:54:52-07:00","id":864829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864631#post864631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being not as up on my Wraith lore as I perhaps should be, the book did get me thinking, &quot;Do wraiths have any defense against necromancy other than 'kill Necromancer immediately'?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Head over to the Wraith forums for a long discussion on this.<br /> <br /> Short version: It depends heavily on the Wraith. While they can all be compelled to some degree, there are a LOT more Wraiths, and a lot more old Wraiths, than there are Vampires. Even with medium-level arcanoi, available to mid-tier Legion shmucks, you can tear down the walls of a vampires haven, rot his body, puppeteer his ghouls, turn his dreams into nightmares, etc. Five-dot powers are things like &quot;rip soul out of body&quot;, &quot;rip soul out of body, insert your own&quot;, &quot;punch agrravated damage form beyond the Veil&quot;, and my personal favourite: &quot;alter someone's fate&quot;. Worst comes to worst, you could always get the Shadow-eaten involved. <br /> <br /> And woe betide any necromancer who pushes the wrong wraith and then enters the Shadowlands. Soulforging is not nice, kids <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I dont know how TTBH handles it, but the Shadowlands belong to the dead, through and through, and even in the metaplot of Wraith, Enoch was an insignificant annoyance until some egyptian shit-stirrer cashed in a cheque. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:29:39-07:00","id":864844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864829#post864829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know how TTBH handles it, but the Shadowlands belong to the dead, through and through, and even in the metaplot of Wraith, Enoch was an insignificant annoyance until some egyptian shit-stirrer cashed in a cheque.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the book, most wraiths don't even know it exists. Those in the Hierarchy who do know it exists are trying to find it, because having vampiric necromancers on their turf makes them deeply uncomfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:48:23-07:00","id":864853,"title":"","content":"It's a little unclear, but in Black Hand, the Hierarchy occupied Enoch prior to the Fourth Great Malestrom, because Enoch is a natural haven in the Tempest and a fortress-city. After the combined might of the Hand took the city back, the Smiling Lord deemed it militarily infeasible to reoccupy, especially with the necromancers entrenched. After WWII, this position is even more tenuous. So they're looking, but maybe not as hard as they really could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:59:49-07:00","id":864856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864476#post864476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 49, just in the section called Bloodlines of the Hand at the Information Age entry. It's clearly stated that the Drakaina are a bloodline distinct from the Harbingers who just happens to be listed after them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You're right, one could read that like they are a bloodline. But it can also be read like they are just a distinct group of Harbingers, since the antitribu are listed together with the clans, and most are just a social distinction, not true bloodlines.But it is ambiguous, and at this point I'd much prefer the Drakaina to be a true bloodline created by the Harbingers' Embraced witches, even if the idea only got to me by reading others interpretation of the text in this thread, which is good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:02:22-07:00","id":864860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864853#post864853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little unclear, but in Black Hand, the Hierarchy occupied Enoch prior to the Fourth Great Malestrom, because Enoch is a natural haven in the Tempest and a fortress-city. After the combined might of the Hand took the city back, the Smiling Lord deemed it militarily infeasible to reoccupy, especially with the necromancers entrenched. After WWII, this position is even more tenuous. So they're looking, but maybe not as hard as they really could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it during the 4th GM that the Black Hand retook it? Cause I can see no other way for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:08:33-07:00","id":864867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864733#post864733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do is understand this correctly that the &quot;Cult&quot; Background cost two points per point (the test is not very clear written imo)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree: this Background is very poorly written. The phrase &quot;require twice the effort to build or accumulate&quot; is unnecessarily vague but suggests that it does cost 2 Background dots or 2 Freebie points for every dot in Cult. I also think in play, the Storyteller would be justified in asking for twice the effort from the PC if/when they try to improve or expand their cult.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864733#post864733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And can you purchase points in the included Backgrounds on top of it? (For example having personal Herd on top having a Cult?)</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, yes. Personally, I wouldn't allow it: it seems clear that Cult is meant to be used as a kind of &quot;umbrella&quot; Background.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:17:54-07:00","id":864871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864867#post864867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree: this Background is very poorly written. The phrase &quot;require twice the effort to build or accumulate&quot; is unnecessarily vague but suggests that it does cost 2 Background dots or 2 Freebie points for every dot in Cult. I also think in play, the Storyteller would be justified in asking for twice the effort from the PC if/when they try to improve or expand their cult.<br /> <br /> As written, yes. Personally, I wouldn't allow it: it seems clear that Cult is meant to be used as a kind of &quot;umbrella&quot; Background.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be worth adding your concerns to the errata thread if you've not already done so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T06:27:22-07:00","id":864877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864871#post864871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It may be worth adding your concerns to the errata thread if you've not already done so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the tip, I will. I should add that I like the premise of the Background. I think I get what the author was going for, but I'd like to see the rules clarified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T07:04:48-07:00","id":864900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864733#post864733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which roles are effected by the Berserker Merit? Ony Attack and Parry or also Damage and Soak rolls or even combat related discipline powers? (And isn't this Merit completely overpowered?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Another vaguely-written power. The phrase &quot;all combat rolls except for dodges&quot; is insufficient, but after re-reading &quot;Combat Systems&quot; (<i>VtM 20th</i>, p. 271) I think the author probably intended for the Merit to apply to the following rolls:<br /> <br /> Close Combat (Dexterity + Brawl/Melee)<br /> Ranged Combat (Dexterity + Athletics/Firearms)<br /> The manoeuvres found on p. 274-280<br /> <br /> Even with that narrow interpretation (i.e. I excluded damage rolls, soak rolls and any kind of Discipline) it's still overpowered. This Merit should be re-examined, clarified and have a more balanced cost/benefit.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T07:21:28-07:00","id":864915,"title":"","content":"two other questions:<br /> <br /> Is the dot in &quot;True Black Hand Membership&quot; (mentioned in the Box &quot;Cult&quot;) free?<br /> <br /> Are required Backgrounds free? The text &quot;Elder Beasts&quot; says so, but it isn't mentioned in the Background section of the character creation part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864900#post864900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with that narrow interpretation (i.e. I excluded damage rolls, soak rolls and any kind of Discipline) it's still overpowered. This Merit should be re-examined, clarified and have a more balanced cost/benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyting that reduces diffculties is very powerfull, and I don't think that there was ever something that reduced the diffculty by -3. Even with just -1 this merit would be good.<br /> But at it is written it is an absolute must have for every fighter concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 04-13-2016, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T07:43:24-07:00","id":864930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864915#post864915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the dot in &quot;True Black Hand Membership&quot; (mentioned in the Box &quot;Cult&quot;) free? Are required Backgrounds free? The text &quot;Elder Beasts&quot; says so, but it isn't mentioned in the Background section of the character creation part.</div> </div> </div> </div>After re-reading both the &quot;New Background: Cult&quot; section on p. 50 and the &quot;Elder Beasts&quot; section on p. 52, I think that a Neonate Tal'Mahe'Ra character would have to pay for one dot in True Black Hand Membership themselves. Page 50 says, &quot;members of the Sect have a minimum one dot in True Black Hand Membership (...)&quot; so it seems to be mandatory for everyone. If one is creating an older character (Ancilla/Elder/Seraphim), the dots come for free as shown on pages 52-53.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864915#post864915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyting that reduces diffculties is very powerfull, and I don't think that there was ever something that reduced the diffculty by -3. Even with just -1 this merit would be good. But at it is written it is an absolute must have for every fighter concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:20:52-07:00","id":864955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864930#post864930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After re-reading both the &quot;New Background: Cult&quot; section on p. 50 and the &quot;Elder Beasts&quot; section on p. 52, I think that a Neonate Tal'Mahe'Ra character would have to pay for one dot in True Black Hand Membership themselves. Page 50 says, &quot;members of the Sect have a minimum one dot in True Black Hand Membership (...)&quot; so it seems to be mandatory for everyone. If one is creating an older character (Ancilla/Elder/Seraphim), the dots come for free as shown on pages 52-53.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would mean that you would have to spend 4 of your 5 background points for requirements.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:32:50-07:00","id":864963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864575#post864575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM is not LEGOs. And if VtM was LEGOs, it would be one of the &quot;built this thing from that movie&quot; kits. Not the big box of bricks to enjoy with nothing but your imagination and physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I love the &quot;build this thing from that movie&quot; sets because they have the most interesting and unique pieces, which I can than use to build something way the fuck cooler and better than either the thing on the box or what I could have done with generic bricks. That's pretty much my approach to gaming as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T09:22:48-07:00","id":864989,"title":"","content":"LEGO was my childhood frustration, I could almost hear the pieces say: &quot;Give up, already. You'll never be an ST. Take a sheet and start drawing dots.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T09:31:15-07:00","id":864998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864955#post864955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would mean that you would have to spend 4 of your 5 background points for requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm reading the creation rules correctly, then yes: Alternate Identity 2, Black Hand Membership 1 and Mentor 1. They must also start with a Willpower rating of at least five. However, a neonate Tal'Mahe'Ra also starts at 10th Generation, the equivalent of three dots in the Generation Background, so it almost evens out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T11:33:12-07:00","id":865034,"title":"","content":"So, with Black Hand book turning to the kraina system, is Rites of Blood &quot;everything is the same discipline&quot; structure no longer canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:13:08-07:00","id":865072,"title":"","content":"One small question, after reading TMR. Perhaps I missed it, or perhaps it's been discussed in an actual Mummy book from at least 10 years ago (too lazy to track that down), I don't know. Anyway, they've established that mummies are immune to vampire blood... in V20, do vampires get anything out of feeding on a mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7242-velvet-elvis","name":"Velvet Elvis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:14:08-07:00","id":865074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=865034#post865034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with Black Hand book turning to the kraina system, is Rites of Blood &quot;everything is the same discipline&quot; structure no longer canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good question...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:15:20-07:00","id":865076,"title":"","content":"I have gone and bought the PDF. I couldn't wait. I hate myself. My bank balance hates me even more...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-15-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:25:30-07:00","id":865085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864437#post864437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Abyssal Exalted shout-out time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have thoughts about this, as a matter of fact. There's a notion that Enoch's Citadel of Ubar may rest within (or upon) a much older ghost city, that below lies a labyrinth of catacombs, that above moves a ghostly 'doomsday clock' of dubious provenance, that the ruling seats are an Ivory Throne and a Basalt Throne...<br /> <br /> Consider that the Underworld city of Stygia from the Second Age was built upon an opening to the Labyrinth, with the Calendar of Setesh moving above the old palace of the Dual Monarchy that included one ruler dressed in white and the other in black...<br /> <br /> Eh, I'm likely reading too much into this, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:36:31-07:00","id":865091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=865085#post865085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have thoughts about this, as a matter of fact. There's a notion that Enoch's Citadel of Ubar may rest within (or upon) a much older ghost city, that below lies a labyrinth of catacombs, that above moves a ghostly 'doomsday clock' of dubious provenance, that the ruling seats are an Ivory Throne and a Basalt Throne...<br /> <br /> Consider that the Underworld city of Stygia from the Second Age was built upon an opening to the Labyrinth, with the Calendar of Setesh moving above the old palace of the Dual Monarchy that included one ruler dressed in white and the other in black...<br /> <br /> Eh, I'm likely reading too much into this, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. It feels like a definite easter egg without saying anything too definite. Personally, I view Exalted as occurring apart from and parallel to any given WoD game, since it allows for a fun thought exercise of characters in a given game who are the equivalent of the Exalted splat - Imbued who resemble Solar characters, Garou and Fera who resemble some Lunars, etc. An Elseworlds concept that does much to expand entertainment... though I do have to say, Sidereals get along much, much better with everyone than Mage does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:38:37-07:00","id":865094,"title":"","content":"Regarding bloodlines not appearing here, I'd say that the omission of the Molochim Baali is more glaring than the missing neo-Lamia Drakaina, if only for how many words are spent on each of these groups and their respective importance to the overall direction of the book. Much is made of these Baali being different from their kin, and I'd think they deserve more recognition than they receive.<br /> <br /> The inclusion of the Maeghar \u2013 while brilliant in a much larger context \u2013 feels 'tacked on' to me without much else to support their inclusion in the book beyond the Rule of Cool. Know that I offer this with full knowledge that the original <i>Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat</i> felt like it included the Kiasyd for even more dubious reasons, but I offer this of provide some perspective on discussions of what's needed or not needed in this book. Regardless, I'm not one to complain about naff inclusions when it comes to the Black Hand!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:40:00-07:00","id":865096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Velvet Elvis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=865072#post865072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One small question, after reading TMR. Perhaps I missed it, or perhaps it's been discussed in an actual Mummy book from at least 10 years ago (too lazy to track that down), I don't know. Anyway, they've established that mummies are immune to vampire blood... in V20, do vampires get anything out of feeding on a mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the V20 book is nothing about mummies, but according to <b>Mummy: The Resurrection </b>(p.204), the blood of an Amenti is so potent that a vampire gets two blood points for every point drained from a mummy. No side effects are mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4081-thomas-weinbrenner","name":"Thomas Weinbrenner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T15:10:35-07:00","id":865131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=865076#post865076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have in and bought the PDF. I couldn't wait. I hate myself. My bank balance hates me even more...</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. And yes, this is Alqamar from the Fomorian Project, known elsewhere as Fabi\u00e1n. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T15:17:13-07:00","id":865138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=865094#post865094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding bloodlines not appearing here, I'd say that the omission of the Molochim Baali is more glaring than the missing neo-Lamia Drakaina, if only for how many words are spent on each of these groups and their respective importance to the overall direction of the book. Much is made of these Baali being different from their kin, and I'd think they deserve more recognition than they receive.<br /> <br /> The inclusion of the Maeghar \u2013 while brilliant in a much larger context \u2013 feels 'tacked on' to me without much else to support their inclusion in the book beyond the Rule of Cool. Know that I offer this with full knowledge that the original <i>Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat</i> felt like it included the Kiasyd for even more dubious reasons, but I offer this of provide some perspective on discussions of what's needed or not needed in this book. Regardless, I'm not one to complain about naff inclusions when it comes to the Black Hand!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree wholeheartily; I miss more information on the Molochim Baali, and I feel the Maeghar (while being quite cool) are not so important as to deserve a two-page spread. On the other hand, I have always loved the Lamiae and I would love to know more about the Drakaina...<br /> <br /> [Possible Spoilers!]<br /> <br /> All in all, the Maeghar don't sound very different from the Kiasyd as they were in DA20 (yes, I know about the different Disciplines, etc...). Basically, it looks like 'Marconius wanted all / the only Kiasyd in existence to be those from his brood, and he tried to kill the rest of them&quot;) (quite typical Lasombra behaviour, on the other hand). Those that weren't murdered hid in the TMR. End of the story.<br /> <br /> [End of Possible Spoilers!]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 04-13-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T04:15:56-07:00","id":865407,"title":"","content":"This is the one supplement I've anticipated the most since... the old forums and the release of V20. Man did we nag about a new proper book on Tal'Mahe'Ra. And now it is here. Haven't dived into the advance pdf yet since I'm a conservative PoD-person. Nothing beats the feeling of a physical book. So what am I doing in this thread you ask? Well, just joining in with MrGones cheering. That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"