19ra?p=865407#post865407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the one supplement I've anticipated the most since... the old forums and the release of V20. Man did we nag about a new proper book on Tal'Mahe'Ra. And now it is here. Haven't dived into the advance pdf yet since I'm a conservative PoD-person. Nothing beats the feeling of a physical book. So what am I doing in this thread you ask? Well, just joining in with MrGones cheering. That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I appreciate it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T18:27:10-07:00","id":865770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=865096#post865096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the V20 book is nothing about mummies, but according to <b>Mummy: The Resurrection </b>(p.204), the blood of an Amenti is so potent that a vampire gets two blood points for every point drained from a mummy. No side effects are mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a while since I last read the book, but I seem to remember that vampires gained temporary Humanity points from drinking Mummy blood, which could cause all sorts of psychology problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T10:44:05-07:00","id":866008,"title":"","content":"This is an advance PDF, but is it too late to put forth any editing errors? I saw a few of them already, but with the PoD book coming out relatively soon I'm worried it might be too late to fix them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, I just saw the stickified errata thread.<br /> <br /> Thusly, and for good measure:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:72px\">DERP</span><br /> <br /> Now that that's done, it's time to go to work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 04-15-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:44:01-07:00","id":866129,"title":"","content":"So, reading the sections on the Archdukes of Hell and the Children of the Outer Darkness, it seems like both the original VTDA clanbook version of the Baali pantheon and the more recent retcons that came in the wake of DTF are now both true?<br /> <br /> The separation of the Children into physical bodies in unnatural tombs and their spirits wandering landscapes of pain and murder makes me think a lot of the Malfeans. It suggests, at least to me, that the physical bodies of the Neverborn sleep in the ground, while their souls sleep in the Labyrinth. Or, perhaps, like the masters of the Nephandi, the bodies of the Sleepers are just potrusions into this world of the Malfeans' dreams.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else have any thoughts about how the Children fit into the scheme of things? I must say, I much prefer them being eldritch, Cthulhoid creatures rather than just Earthbound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:49:52-07:00","id":866131,"title":"","content":"Mind you, I think we've lost something by having the Molochim and the Swarm merged. IIRC, the Swarm was a third faction of the Baali, perhaps descended from the Unnamed One. They carried literal swarms within their bodies, which was kinda cool, and exceedingly disgusting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T15:11:47-07:00","id":866139,"title":"","content":"I'm conflicted, as I thought the Earthbound connection worked pretty well and I'm puzzled by Lovecraftean monsters being incinerated when exposed to the sun. (That makes it sound like the Children are antediluvians or perhaps prehistoric non-Cainite vampires rather than extra-dimensional horrors.) But the disturbing people's dreams and warping reality near their tombs as they grow wakeful fits. In any event, the matter is left ambiguous enough that it should work for a variety of campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T17:12:35-07:00","id":866174,"title":"","content":"I'm just pleased I found easter egg references to Chicago by Night, D.C. by Night and Montreal by Night in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T23:49:33-07:00","id":866288,"title":"","content":"I finished to read the Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra yesterday. In general, I liked. It has an abundant background and metaplot, with some mistakes of detail, but in general I think it's an improvement since Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, it's ok.<br /> <br /> Now, there are some big things I disagree with.<br /> <br /> The real origin of the Nagaraja. I think it's more credible the original version as a failed intent to get the inmortality, not cannon fodder (a neonate vampire is not better than a experienced mage) for the Idran in their war with the vampires.<br /> <br /> In the description of the clans of the Tal'Mahe'Ra (Harbingers of Skulls, Old Clan Tzimisce, Nagaraja, Maeghar), Where are the True Brujah? I would add a short description (a few lines for each one) about the presence and position of other clans in the Hand (antitribu Assamites, the Ventrue of Cretheus, Toreador, Gangrel et all).<br /> <br /> About the Maeghar. I think they were a bad idea in DAV20 and they are a bad idea now, and I think the Tal'Mahe'Ra is not a place for them. Their presence seems forced.<br /> <br /> About the rules: I like the arcaic sorcery of the Idran, a coherent point of view in their isolation of the Traditions. I dislike the kraina of Koldunism. The kraina of Enoch is Necromancy and the kraina of the Well is Dark Thaumaturgy. A type of blood magic shouldn't encompass the domain of others.<br /> <br /> And the last chapter, the Chronicle of Tal'Mahe'Ra...it's horrible, the worst part of the book (A ghoul or whatever with Auspex 8, Dementation 9, Fortitude 9? Please...It's a joke). A bizarre story that breaks the spirit of the background of the book. And the statistics and features of the characters at the end should be revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2250,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","user":"Magus","date":". 04-16-2016, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T00:04:46-07:00","id":866291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866129#post866129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, reading the sections on the Archdukes of Hell and the Children of the Outer Darkness, it seems like both the original VTDA clanbook version of the Baali pantheon and the more recent retcons that came in the wake of DTF are now both true?<br /> <br /> The separation of the Children into physical bodies in unnatural tombs and their spirits wandering landscapes of pain and murder makes me think a lot of the Malfeans. It suggests, at least to me, that the physical bodies of the Neverborn sleep in the ground, while their souls sleep in the Labyrinth. Or, perhaps, like the masters of the Nephandi, the bodies of the Sleepers are just potrusions into this world of the Malfeans' dreams.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else have any thoughts about how the Children fit into the scheme of things? I must say, I much prefer them being eldritch, Cthulhoid creatures rather than just Earthbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on I thought the idea was that the Children of the Outer Darkness that the Baali worship were already tied to the Neverborn Malfeans of Wraith and the Outer Lords of Mage?<br /> <br /> In so far as the &quot;dead&quot; Children that did not &quot;hide in the earth&quot; become the Neverborn. Meanwhile the &quot;dreams&quot; of both the dead and &quot;living&quot; Children formed the Outer Lords of the Deep Umbra. The Children that survived the utterance of &quot;Let there be light!&quot; were the big-bad things like Kupala and such.<br /> <br /> At least I thought this was, if not outright stated, then pretty heavily hinted at across Vampire, Wraith and Mage fluff before Demon the Fallen came out. Maybe that's just me remembering the subtext as text though, been ages since I reread the Baali fluff. Alternatively, might just be me remembering that as cannon because it was the case in the games I played in/ran years ago.<br /> <br /> Damn...stupid fallible memory. <br /> <br /> Still if Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra does make that &quot;text&quot; for new fluff I'll be happy. Even more so if it can clean up/integrate the <i>&quot;the Baali actually worship the Earthbound because Demon says so&quot;</i> fluff-up that occurred late in Revised Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T01:01:50-07:00","id":866307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866131#post866131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I think we've lost something by having the Molochim and the Swarm merged. IIRC, the Swarm was a third faction of the Baali, perhaps descended from the Unnamed One. They carried literal swarms within their bodies, which was kinda cool, and exceedingly disgusting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Swarm being the progeny of the Unnamed comes from Road of Sin; in the Baali clanbook, the Swarm was one of the orders Moloch founded, a sect in the bloodline.<br /> <br /> So it's more choosing among the canon options rather than a retcon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T01:35:54-07:00","id":866311,"title":"","content":"I'm profoundly miffed that the Old Clan have now bound Kupala rather than worshiping it. That's a pretty significant departure from the original fluff, and not one that I like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T03:31:17-07:00","id":866334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=865096#post865096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the V20 book is nothing about mummies, but according to <b>Mummy: The Resurrection </b>(p.204), the blood of an Amenti is so potent that a vampire gets two blood points for every point drained from a mummy. No side effects are mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Just jumping in as I noted this while skimming through -- a similar comment/discussion was taking place elsewhere relative to this...)<br /> <br /> pg.204 only deals with the &quot;simple overview&quot; of vampires relative to Mummy as a game; if you jump over to pg.145 (&quot;Lifeblood&quot;), it covers how Amenti vitae has a powerful (and for many undead, disturbing) effect when they drink it -- it temporarily restores their (H)umanity, even for those who mystically/spiritually are set down a very different path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T04:39:10-07:00","id":866341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866311#post866311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm profoundly miffed that the Old Clan have now bound Kupala rather than worshiping it. That's a pretty significant departure from the original fluff, and not one that I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Transylvania by Night the Tzimisce are depicted as using Koldunic Sorcery to suppress Kupala and his minions, going as far as to use Koldunic Sorcery to weaken the barrier to the Umbra on Kupala's Night and slaughter his spirit-minions. So it's not really a retcon, just a resurfacing of earlier material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11489-cynical-cat","name":"Cynical Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T08:54:21-07:00","id":866401,"title":"","content":"I had never liked the original idea of the spiritual world, Enoch and other stories of the black hand, close to fantasy. But after many years I did with the book Dirty Secrets of Black hand to complete my collection of Sabbat books. And in part I liked. Except everything related with Enoch and the spiritual world. So I decided to give a chance to this new version. And the truth was disappointed enough. Except for the very few ideas. I can not find the Gothic-Punk feeling. It is not very well structured for reading. Perhaps the number of authors seems excessive. I think they're 13, and I guess everyone would want to offer the best of him. So the result is a goodbye to personal horror, and hello to the fantastic world. I enjoyed the chapter of the Bahari (Although not everything in it) and Aralu. Alternative ideas that are actually Aralu leave many options open. But I definitely prefer and fits more with the history of clan Tzimisce the idea of \u200b\u200bthe Shadow Crusade than all this new issue of infernalism and Assaku. The Maeghar seems like a horrible idea. It seems they are stuck in the book forcefully. I understand that the True Brujah are being written in the new book of the bloodlines. But still, it would have been nice to include them. The chronicle of the final chapter seems to me ridiculous. Much worse than Dust to Dust... and I'm not talking about the art of the characters, because I have nothing good to say. I also miss the ghoul families in the book, but I guess they were not included, for the same reason that the True Brujah.<br /> I was expecting something else, after reading various opinions about it. I guess I'll stick with the most hated version of Steven C. brown.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/Classic%20World%20of%20Darkness/1991~Vampire%20The%20Masquerade/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=Variant-Gangrel~Country%20Gangrel.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/Classic%20World%20of%20Darkness/1991~Vampire%20The%20Masquerade/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=Sect-variant~Sabbat.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/861-pierre","name":"Pierre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar861_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T09:48:08-07:00","id":866425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=864915#post864915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">two other questions:<br /> <br /> Is the dot in &quot;True Black Hand Membership&quot; (mentioned in the Box &quot;Cult&quot;) free?<br /> <br /> Are required Backgrounds free? The text &quot;Elder Beasts&quot; says so, but it isn't mentioned in the Background section of the character creation part.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I could be misremembering, but I believe the minimum ratings are intended to be. Might be something to mention in the errata thread as needing a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T16:10:51-07:00","id":866555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866291#post866291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hang on I thought the idea was that the Children of the Outer Darkness that the Baali worship were already tied to the Neverborn Malfeans of Wraith and the Outer Lords of Mage?<br /> <br /> In so far as the &quot;dead&quot; Children that did not &quot;hide in the earth&quot; become the Neverborn. Meanwhile the &quot;dreams&quot; of both the dead and &quot;living&quot; Children formed the Outer Lords of the Deep Umbra. The Children that survived the utterance of &quot;Let there be light!&quot; were the big-bad things like Kupala and such.<br /> <br /> At least I thought this was, if not outright stated, then pretty heavily hinted at across Vampire, Wraith and Mage fluff before Demon the Fallen came out. Maybe that's just me remembering the subtext as text though, been ages since I reread the Baali fluff. Alternatively, might just be me remembering that as cannon because it was the case in the games I played in/ran years ago.<br /> <br /> Damn...stupid fallible memory. <br /> <br /> Still if Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra does make that &quot;text&quot; for new fluff I'll be happy. Even more so if it can clean up/integrate the <i>&quot;the Baali actually worship the Earthbound because Demon says so&quot;</i> fluff-up that occurred late in Revised Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they were Malfean-like beings in VTDA (well, in Clanbook: Baali, anyway). It was DTF that retconned them into Earthbound. I always liked the VTDA mythos better, because it wasn't too heavily tied to a Judeo-Christian paradigm. Or rather, it could be considered more Gnostic and Qlippothic than the DTF alternative, at least.<br /> <br /> TBHAGttTMR presents both options. So DTF fans can have their characters deal with the Archdukes and their minions, and Cb:Baali fans can deal with Cthulhoid nasties instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-16-2016, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T16:14:24-07:00","id":866557,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was never a big fan of &quot;Twist! The Satanist seeming vampires we told you actually worshipped alien gods, actually WERE worshipping fallen Judeo-Christian Angels after all!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T17:11:48-07:00","id":866576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866311#post866311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm profoundly miffed that the Old Clan have now bound Kupala rather than worshiping it. That's a pretty significant departure from the original fluff, and not one that I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Cynical Cat notes, it does hearken back to the treatment in <i>Transylvania by Night</i>. It also helps reconcile my personal Old Clan Tzimisce character's support of the Sabbat Inquisition with the setting rather than making his entire bloodline a bunch of demon-worshipers that he'd be at odds with, which seemed to be the direction <i>Rites of the Blood</i> was heading in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:40:09-07:00","id":866697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866557#post866557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was never a big fan of &amp;quot;Twist! The Satanist seeming vampires we told you actually worshipped alien gods, actually WERE worshipping fallen Judeo-Christian Angels after all!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And the premise for why they were keeping the Children quiescent was also a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:06:14-07:00","id":866936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866129#post866129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, reading the sections on the Archdukes of Hell and the Children of the Outer Darkness, it seems like both the original VTDA clanbook version of the Baali pantheon and the more recent retcons that came in the wake of DTF are now both true?<br /> <br /> The separation of the Children into physical bodies in unnatural tombs and their spirits wandering landscapes of pain and murder makes me think a lot of the Malfeans. It suggests, at least to me, that the physical bodies of the Neverborn sleep in the ground, while their souls sleep in the Labyrinth. Or, perhaps, like the masters of the Nephandi, the bodies of the Sleepers are just potrusions into this world of the Malfeans' dreams.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else have any thoughts about how the Children fit into the scheme of things? I must say, I much prefer them being eldritch, Cthulhoid creatures rather than just Earthbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to pretend that Demon: The Fallen doesn't exist, and entertain the possibility that the Children are Antedeluvian vampires. It would be delightfully ironic if, by laboring to keep the Children asleep, the Molochim Baali were the ones who have been inadvertently doing the most to prevent Gehenna all these years. Maybe the Clans are unaware of the real reason they've been led to despise the Molochim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 04-17-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:01:52-07:00","id":866970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866936#post866936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like to pretend that Demon: The Fallen doesn't exist, and entertain the possibility that the Children are Antedeluvian vampires. It would be delightfully ironic if, by laboring to keep the Children asleep, the Molochim Baali were the ones who have been inadvertently doing the most to prevent Gehenna all these years. Maybe the Clans are unaware of the real reason they've been led to despise the Molochim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clans despise the Baali because Baali are the stinking satanists and you are supposed to be a good christian. It doesn't matter if you mind control patients into killing themselves (how does Netchurch has Humanity 6 again?) or fleshcraft chairs or go on a murder spree against the Nosferatu (fuck you, Ferox, you are the worst character) - demon worshiping is just always worse. Because considering what Baali actually do, there is seriously nothing that's worse than what Camarilla or Sabbat casually do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:31:00-07:00","id":866992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866311#post866311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm profoundly miffed that the Old Clan have now bound Kupala rather than worshiping it. That's a pretty significant departure from the original fluff, and not one that I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned in terms of 'adding what we already had' I'd say that this, too, links to the treatment of the Path of the Hive from <i>Chaining the Beast</i>, where the Baali connexion to the (Old Clan) Tzimisce and Kupala is pretty much spelled out as we see here. It's kinda neat to see that notion come back, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866129#post866129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The separation of the Children into physical bodies in unnatural tombs and their spirits wandering landscapes of pain and murder makes me think a lot of the Malfeans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always felt \u2014 even BEFORE reading <b>Exalted</b>'s <i>The Abyssals</i> \u2014 that the Children of the Baali where the Neverborn who didn't die. The Neverborn of the Malfeans are the ghosts of the Sleepers the Baail venerate, protect, what have you. In this, I didn't see anything wonky. However, that does contradict anything in <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> or what we see in the <b>Dark Ages</b> book <i>Devil's Due</i>. AND the discussion of the 'Dukes of Hell' in both <i>V20 Black Hand: a Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</i> and in <i>Rites of the Blood</i> otherwise conform to the descriptions of Earthbound demons from <b>Demon: the Fallen</b>, so... Uh yeah. There's plenty of room for one's interpretation to go more than one direction.<br /> <br /> No doubt (again!), such things are what *I* love in a book for a game, so don't take my stances as straight-up attacks. Think of them more as jabs to get or keep conversation going!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T13:58:51-07:00","id":867038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=866970#post866970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clans despise the Baali because Baali are the stinking satanists and you are supposed to be a good christian. It doesn't matter if you mind control patients into killing themselves (how does Netchurch has Humanity 6 again?) or fleshcraft chairs or go on a murder spree against the Nosferatu (fuck you, Ferox, you are the worst character) - demon worshiping is just always worse. Because considering what Baali actually do, there is seriously nothing that's worse than what Camarilla or Sabbat casually do.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are actually worse. They do all the bad stuff other vampires do as well as working to bring forth terrible forces on the world which will screw over every other vampire. See that second part of the sentence? It's what most vampires believe about the Baali and in some cases is actually true. That's going to get you on everyone's kill list. But take solace in the fact that Ferox is on the Red List and thus has even worse problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11489-cynical-cat","name":"Cynical Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T14:21:41-07:00","id":867053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynical Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=867038#post867038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they are actually worse. They do all the bad stuff other vampires do as well as working to bring forth terrible forces on the world which will screw over every other vampire. See that second part of the sentence? It's what most vampires believe about the Baali and in some cases is actually true. That's going to get you on everyone's kill list. But take solace in the fact that Ferox is on the Red List and thus has even worse problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tal'Mahe'Ra wants to wake up the Antideluvians, Assamites and Settites revere and want to wake up an Antideluvian, while the Camarilla is built upon screwing over every vampire that is lower ranked than you are and what the Sabbat wants strongly depends on which paragraph of which book you are reading.<br /> <br /> P.S. Ferox being on the Red List in no way makes me hate him less for having Humanity 9, True Faith 9 while being an unrepentant racist serial killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T14:50:23-07:00","id":867072,"title":"","content":"What else do people like about the book? The Bahari inclusion seemed a bit forced to me, as did the Maeghar. The Harbingers were a good fit. The Baali almost fit. In this sense, however, it's as snowflake-friendly as the first book, so it's at least in the spirit of the original.<br /> <br /> I do like the info on the Baali and Harbingers, though. The fluff about Lilith was also interesting. I'd quite like another Book of Nod-style book.<br /> <br /> I like the new take on the Shadow Crusade, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:32:46-07:00","id":867155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=867053#post867053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tal'Mahe'Ra wants to wake up the Antideluvians, Assamites and Settites revere and want to wake up an Antideluvian, while the Camarilla is built upon screwing over every vampire that is lower ranked than you are and what the Sabbat wants strongly depends on which paragraph of which book you are reading.<br /> <br /> P.S. Ferox being on the Red List in no way makes me hate him less for having Humanity 9, True Faith 9 while being an unrepentant racist serial killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, all of the above believe they are serving a higher, nobler goal or protecting the Vampire race, or resisting tyranny, or promoting the greater good. They do bad shit in the name of noble sounding goals that may not actually be noble. Infernalist Baali do terrible things in the service of creating Hell on Earth. There is no way in which the knowing and deliberate service of cosmic evil doesn't generate a bad reaction in all that hear it, no matter who hears it. The Baali are going to carry a bad rep with that from everybody because of that and really have no cause to complain about it. The Setites have a reputation almost as bad and they at least believe that their god is righteous and their cause just.<br /> <br /> Ferox having Humanity 9 is fucked up, but having Truth Faith and an ocean of blood on your hands isn't a problem. We all know what terrible things religious zealots can get up to. And he does, as a member of the Red List, have a far worse reputation than the Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11489-cynical-cat","name":"Cynical Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:56:04-07:00","id":867176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynical Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=867155#post867155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, all of the above believe they are serving a higher, nobler goal or protecting the Vampire race, or resisting tyranny, or promoting the greater good. They do bad shit in the name of noble sounding goals that may not actually be noble.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what, all of Camarilla is totally on board with the goal of waking up Haquim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:45:33-07:00","id":867265,"title":"","content":"I just want to pipe in and say how much I enjoy the New Black Hand Book. <br /> <br /> I particularly like the cleaned up motivation of Old Clan Tzimisce. Previous books have always presented a sort of weird twisted connection to Kupula. In one instance they worship him for providing them with their Koldun sorcery and on the other actively work against his corruption of the land. I was never really sure how the Tzimisce felt about Kupula as the material was contradictory. When Krainas were first presented in V20 Dark Ages I felt the change was unnecessary and jarring. The new fluff, Kupula having corrupted Koldune, fits great with the setting and ads a bit of motivation and mythology that keeps me reading and enjoying VtM. <br /> <br /> The evolution of the Molochites was nice. The text kept to motivations first expressed in DA Clanbook Baali. I've always taken from the Baali Clanbook the reason the Baali keep the Children sleeping was more so they could extract power via Daimoinon without paying the consequences. Their motivation was self interest rather than any form of altruism. With the Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra the Cult although still monstrous, becomes more sympathetic and righteous. They are an Inquisition against Infernalism. (Even though they sacrifice to demons they do so for righteous reasons) An interesting shift since the loss of Moloch.<br /> <br /> I liked the over all tenor of the book. The idea of a Cult made of Cults tenuously held together by their common goal to serve the powers that sleep in the crypts. Entities on whose identity they cannot agree and if seriously debated could split the tenuous alliance. This common theme threaded its way well through most of the book. The story at the beginning of each chapter worked well to highlight the material and brought what was always represented as a Sect of elders to the level of a neonate. <br /> <br /> The weakest portion of the book for me was the inclusion of the Megher, Golconda and Diablorie. Positively, I liked the expansion of the system for both Golconda and Diablorie for those STs who wish to include either in their game. Until the rules section, however neither Daiblorie nor Golconda had previously received a jot of attention. Their inclusion just felt out of place. As I said I liked the write up for both but thought they would have fit better in a different book. <br /> <br /> As for the Megher I just felt they were superfluous. Unlike the other clans and bloodlines they weren't as entwined within the overall text and reason for inclusion was never really expressed in the overall narrative. It was nice that there was a tie in to V20 DA but they may have better served as a template like abominations rather than as a full bloodline. <br /> <br /> As an aside I hope the Bloodlines book ties in the fluff of Lamia surviving from V20 and their recreation (re-embrace) in Tal'Mahe'Ra<br /> <br /> Great book with a lot of material to digest extract and use. I'd like to shout out to Obsidian and the writers for providing a great book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T20:16:57-07:00","id":867316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=867176#post867176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what, all of Camarilla is totally on board with the goal of waking up Haquim?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea why this is your response, but . . .<br /> <br /> 1) The Assamites aren't part of the Camarilla and they aren't loved by them. Al-Ashrad's faction that joined were the ones that weren't into it. <br /> <br /> 2) The Camarilla's position is that the Antideluvians are mythical or dead so the Assamite ancestor worship is (from a Camarilla point of view) meaningless and Haquim isn't a threat. Unlike say the very real and alive terrible cosmic evil the Infernalist Baali serve.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every culture and religion which has a conception of a cosmic evil from Zoarastrism to Navajo traditional beliefs treats those who willingly serve it as objects of horror and revulsion. This isn't a Christian thing, it's a fairly universal human response to the idea of serving pure evil. In the real world, demon worshipers and witches are pretty much products of human imagination. In Vampire, both the Baali and the evil they serve are real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11489-cynical-cat","name":"Cynical Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T01:13:35-07:00","id":867430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynical Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=867316#post867316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea why this is your response, but . . .<br /> <br /> 1) The Assamites aren't part of the Camarilla and they aren't loved by them. Al-Ashrad's faction that joined were the ones that weren't into it.<br /> <br /> 2) The Camarilla's position is that the Antideluvians are mythical or dead so the Assamite ancestor worship is (from a Camarilla point of view) meaningless and Haquim isn't a threat. Unlike say the very real and alive terrible cosmic evil the Infernalist Baali serve.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every culture and religion which has a conception of a cosmic evil from Zoarastrism to Navajo traditional beliefs treats those who willingly serve it as objects of horror and revulsion. This isn't a Christian thing, it's a fairly universal human response to the idea of serving pure evil. In the real world, demon worshipers and witches are pretty much products of human imagination. In Vampire, both the Baali and the evil they serve are real.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my response because both Assamites and Settites are worshiping ancient evil, which vampires who are not Assassmites or Settites don't want to wake up. And yet Baali are killed on sight, and those two aren't.<br /> Are you seriously telling me that Camarilla vampires would rather believe in Satan rather than very old vampires existing? Seriously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T03:01:48-07:00","id":867460,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla believes the Antideluvians are dead or gone. The Setites and Asssamites make themselves useful to Camarilla Vampires. That's not true of the evil the Baali serve or the perception of the Baali Clan. They're viewed as dangerous as the evil they serve as being very real. Is that unfair to some of them? Probably. <br /> <br /> And yes, since most Vampires believed they are descended by Cain who was cursed by God, they are quite willing to believe in the Devil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11489-cynical-cat","name":"Cynical Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T05:20:20-07:00","id":867499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=867430#post867430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my response because both Assamites and Settites are worshiping ancient evil, which vampires who are not Assassmites or Settites don't want to wake up. And yet Baali are killed on sight, and those two aren't.<br /> Are you seriously telling me that Camarilla vampires would rather believe in Satan rather than very old vampires existing? Seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div>How much of Setite and Assamite Lore do you suspect the main body of the Camarilla knows? <br /> <br /> As far as most Kindred are concerned, Setites are a strange bunch with an equally strange faith - but they don't preach their hatred of every other Clan from street corners, so where's the harm?<br /> <br /> Most Camarilla likely buy into the Assamites role as independent mercs for hire, completely apathetic to any religion or personal cause the Assamite may follow. <br /> <br /> The Baali represent an unrepentant, historically known threat. They are bogeymen, discussed in Elysia. Easy to do when most of them are dead. Satan is a known quantity among human believers, so given that all vampires were once human, of course they'll target infernalists over a group worshiping some guy named Haqim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:19:59-07:00","id":867576,"title":"","content":"There's also the very pragmatic matter than the Assamites and Followers of Set are full clans, who've been doing quite well for themselves without the benefits of sect membership for the last 500 years. Destroying the occasional solitary devil worshiper doesn't carry the same political and tactical risks as destroying members of a fairly close-knit group of thousands of vampires, many of them quite ancient and powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:32:15-07:00","id":867582,"title":"","content":"I have enjoyed this book and what they did with the organization. I am stoked that what was once mentioned for the Baali in the DA Clanbook is now talked about in detail. I think it opens up all kinds of possibilities for stories and characters.<br /> <br /> I also like that it is potentially a house of cards waiting to fall. Don't even need to mention the whole Noddist/Bahari split/fusion, but like what happens if the Sleepers/Children of the Outer Dark are really Antediluvians (come on, one burned in the sun when the First Tribe dug it up!), and that Asakku are nothing more than the Eldest taking over? Wouldn't that throw a wrench in their plans of working for the Antediluvians?<br /> <br /> Or what if this is exactly what the Old Clan and Order of Moloch already know/believe and they are hiding in plain sight, using the Tal'Mahe'Ra? This is just what's been in my recent thoughts, there are so many other possibilities, man I wish I had a gaming group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11149,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","user":"PJ123","date":". 04-18-2016, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:43:30-07:00","id":867620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=867576#post867576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the very pragmatic matter than the Assamites and Followers of Set are full clans, who've been doing quite well for themselves without the benefits of sect membership for the last 500 years. Destroying the occasional solitary devil worshiper doesn't carry the same political and tactical risks as destroying members of a fairly close-knit group of thousands of vampires, many of them quite ancient and powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is above all political organization. Their governing bodies, from the Primogen council of Ottawa to the Inner Circle of the sect, make decisions based on a mix of pragmatism, precedent and prejudice. Most of the time, the political math favours circumspect dealings with the children of Haquim and Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11585-marcl","name":"MarcL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:11:36-07:00","id":867763,"title":"","content":"Very true. Open war against the Setites and Assamites has happened in the past and it was costly for all sides involved. Stepping on the Baali, on the rare occasions where you can find one, doesn't carry the same risk. Hell, it's one of the things you can all agree on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11489-cynical-cat","name":"Cynical Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T06:14:41-07:00","id":869262,"title":"","content":"Something occurred to me regarding the Diablerie rules: They mesh real nice with the original practices of the Path of Blood. That is, not being wanton but methodical and careful in what you are doing. With the new level 1 Quietus in DAV20, it even makes sense that rather than committing Amaranth (right of destruction to Eldest), they collect the heartsblood and bring it to the Clan Elders. The elders have collections of these and lower the loyal Assamites Generation proportionately, so they are not consumed by one too powerful to Diablerize.<br /> <br /> Even the Path of Caine write-up mentions something about taking the Vitae of unworthy, but temper it. Sure, you could be like Monty and Mithras, but look where that got him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T19:51:36-07:00","id":873480,"title":"","content":"Didn't finished reading the book, but right need I need understand why the protection of humanity is &quot;a pillar of the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra ideology&quot;. Right now, it doesn't make any sense. Is there any rationale behind that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T00:08:34-07:00","id":873569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=873480#post873480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't finished reading the book, but right need I need understand why the protection of humanity is &quot;a pillar of the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra ideology&quot;. Right now, it doesn't make any sense. Is there any rationale behind that?</div> </div> </div> </div>TBH page 41, under the heading 'Pity our Children'. Hand members would give a number of reasons for protecting humanity (treating humanity as a farmer would their cattle, safeguarding them for when the Antediluvians come, believing humanity are Earth's true heirs, the words of Lilith, etc.), but a key part of it is because they're based in the Underworld and work with wraiths, so they can see what happens when humans aren't allowed to settle their business, when they and others waste human lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:18:51-07:00","id":873767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=873569#post873569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> TBH page 41, under the heading 'Pity our Children'. Hand members would give a number of reasons for protecting humanity (treating humanity as a farmer would their cattle, safeguarding them for when the Antediluvians come, believing humanity are Earth's true heirs, the words of Lilith, etc.), but a key part of it is because they're based in the Underworld and work with wraiths, so they can see what happens when humans aren't allowed to settle their business, when they and others waste human lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I have not reached this section of the book.<br /> <br /> All those reasons, however, could act as justifications for protecting the whole humanity, but not individual human beings. I can conceive the True Hand dogma saying &quot;**** these individual humans in particular&quot;, meaning they're still a bunch of monsters that pay lip service to the &quot;protection of humanity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1119,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","user":"Primal Flame","date":". 04-25-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:01:00-07:00","id":873798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=873767#post873767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. I have not reached this section of the book.<br /> <br /> All those reasons, however, could act as justifications for protecting the whole humanity, but not individual human beings. I can conceive the True Hand dogma saying &quot;**** these individual humans in particular&quot;, meaning they're still a bunch of monsters that pay lip service to the &quot;protection of humanity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the Bahari chapter notes that previously, paying lip service to that tenet was what the Hand did, until the Bahari joined up and started holding them to their word, in the name of punishing those who inflict more suffering than they need to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:40:56-07:00","id":873865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=873798#post873798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, the Bahari chapter notes that previously, paying lip service to that tenet was what the Hand did, until the Bahari joined up and started holding them to their word, in the name of punishing those who inflict more suffering than they need to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the Bahari humanists? Honest question, I don't know a lot about them. <br /> <br /> Also, do you know where can I read more on the Bahari, in addition to V20 The Black Hand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:22:22-07:00","id":873893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=873865#post873865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Bahari humanists? Honest question, I don't know a lot about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The groups associated with the Hand... noooot so much. The Bahari pursue gnosis through pain. Their sense of justice isn't so much about compassion or peace, but about teaching through pain and repairing some of Caine's fuck-ups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, do you know where can I read more on the Bahari, in addition to V20 The Black Hand? </div> </div> </div>Er. The only big source I can think of to date is Revelations of the Dark Mother, presenting Lilith's version of the Cainite mythos. The V20 core has the Path of Lilith, V20 Dark Ages has that era's Road of Lilith, and there's a little bit more on the Path in Chaining the Beast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T13:27:52-07:00","id":873987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=873893#post873893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er. The only big source I can think of to date is Revelations of the Dark Mother, presenting Lilith's version of the Cainite mythos. The V20 core has the Path of Lilith, V20 Dark Ages has that era's Road of Lilith, and there's a little bit more on the Path in Chaining the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'll check Chaining the Beast!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:58:21-07:00","id":880387,"title":"","content":"The Indra and the Archaic Sorcerer template in general was my favorite part of the book. I do really want to play one in a vampire game just aligning himself with a coterie or a neonate. The iconoclastic anarch who just need some power beyond what is afforded to him as a neonate suddenly has the chance to get what he lacks with the assistance of this magician, The ambitious vampire who wants to climb up the hierarchy who just needs that ace in a whole or maybe someone who just wants to be an autakris who simply cannot stand on his own. An archaic sorcerer becoming the blood familiar of a young vampire rather than an elder could produce a lot of interesting stories...or just an archaic sorcerer being played...i want to play one....please....anyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:49:27-07:00","id":880495,"title":"","content":"I don't know... it's an interesting theoretical concept, but if I want to play a vampire that uses magic I just buy Thaumaturgy, Necromancy, or Koldunic Sorcery. Between multiple paths and all the rituals available those are plenty versatile for my taste.<br /> <br /> One thing this book has convinced me of is that if I ever storytell a Black Hand game again, Denzel <b>will</b> be a member of the Tal'Mahe'Ra. Not a vampire, or ghoul, or Idran sorcerer, but just a member in good standing because who wouldn't want to be in a club with Denzel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 05-02-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:54:43-07:00","id":883231,"title":"","content":"I don't like what they did with the Path of the Scorched Heart. &quot;Speaking falsely&quot; as level 4 sin for a sect where everybody (according to the rules) has to have a secret identity is completely unplayable imo, and &quot;Relying on others&quot; on level 7 seems also a little bit to low.<br /> <br /> I find it also kind of wired that in sect that is supposed to worship the Antediluvians, the Bahari seem to play such a big role, a that the book is devoting so much space to them.<br /> <br /> And why is there no Path that worships the Antediluvians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T15:51:30-07:00","id":883267,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, is there going to be a physical copy of the book released by RPG game?<br /> <br /> Other than that, I do like the idea of a Path related to the Antediluvians or at least the teachings of Vampire ethics in the Book of Nod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T16:48:01-07:00","id":883296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=883267#post883267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, is there going to be a physical copy of the book released by RPG game?<br /> <br /> Other than that, I do like the idea of a Path related to the Antediluvians or at least the teachings of Vampire ethics in the Book of Nod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should a pagecount really be wasted on something as niche as Path of Ventrue or Path of Absimiliard or whatever? Compared to everything else you can write about, Paths are easy, you can make any Path in about 30 minutes. It's just an arbitrary set of commandments centered around the subject. Here, have an example off the top of my head. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 800px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\"><b>Path of Cocoa</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Conscience/Self-Control</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">10. Failing to brew a pot of cocoa every night, regardless of circumstances</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Cocoa requires dedication</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">9. Failing to instruct other vampires about the virtues of cocoa drinking</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">All vampires must have the opportunity to taste cocoa</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">8. Allowing tea-drinking go unpunished</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Straying from the true path is blasphemous</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">7. Showing disrespect to other drinkers of cocoa</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">True cosiness can not be achieved through rudness</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">6. Spilling a pot of cocoa</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Wastrels can never ascend</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">5. Fearing cocoa</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Cocoa is simply an inevitable step to true cosiness</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">4. Not seeking out new cocoa brands</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">The truth is spread between the tastes; it must be found</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">3. Failing to resist Frenzy</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">The beast doesn't understand the virtue of cocoa</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">2. Murder</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Dead can't drink cocoa</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">1. Refusing an offer to drink cocoa</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">To be one with cocoa one must drink cocoa</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Cuddlies.<br /> <b>Bearing</b><b>:</b> Cosiness. The Cuddlies radiate warmth and fuzziness. The bearing modifier applies to influencing others and even their own Beast (rolls to resist both frenzy and R\u00f6tschreck).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 05-05-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T17:05:59-07:00","id":883312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=883296#post883296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Should a pagecount...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is amazing, I had a good laugh reading the hierarchy of sins. Please do one with Ice Tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T22:26:03-07:00","id":883496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=883296#post883296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a pagecount really be wasted on something as niche as Path of Ventrue or Path of Absimiliard or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a path for every Antediluvians, one for all that describes the belive of the Black Hand.<br /> Maybe you can just take Path of Cain instead (or a variation of it).<br /> And when it comes page count, they used ~25 pages for the Bahari, it would make much more sense imo to use the pages to describe what the majority of the sect belives. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T00:09:33-07:00","id":883531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=883267#post883267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, is there going to be a physical copy of the book released by RPG game?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's going to be a POD version available from DriveThruRPG, but no traditionally printed version (since it wasn't Kickstarted, which is the only way Onyx Path do traditionally printed books).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T06:36:34-07:00","id":883695,"title":"","content":"I would use the DAV20 Road of Blood. It's pretty well lined up with the TMR modus operandi, and even justifiable for non-Assamites to be on, considering the Sect has been working with that Clan almost since its inception.<br /> <br /> As to the Bahari and their beliefs... Some believe the Aralu are Lilith's children. I also have the opinion that some of the TMR are in it to thwart the Antediluvians, sort of hiding in plain sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:47:25-07:00","id":884088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PJ123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=883695#post883695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the Bahari and their beliefs... Some believe the Aralu are Lilith's children. I also have the opinion that some of the TMR are in it to thwart the Antediluvians, sort of hiding in plain sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get why the Bahari are in the Black Hand, but I don't really get the writers made them most influencial fraction and get such a long description.<br /> Especially since afaik the &quot;normal&quot; (Noddists) version is nowhere really covered in the V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:27:50-07:00","id":884222,"title":"","content":"I really didn't see the need to separate the Maeghar from the Kiasyd as something &quot;different&quot; and the additional weakness added to them is just bonkers. Definitely a step backward from the great changes made to Kiasyd for DAV20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T10:58:50-07:00","id":884747,"title":"","content":"The maeghar and the original kiasyd were always different. The dark ages kiasyd thing was not a retconn of the old kiasyd or anything like that at all, but they were probably made to expand the history of the original kiasyd since...The maeghar are avoiding the shit out of them. Also remember that lore of the bloodlines is a book that is coming out that will have a write up of the kiasyd if i remember correctly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T11:12:31-07:00","id":884756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=884747#post884747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The maeghar and the original kiasyd were always different. The dark ages kiasyd thing was not a retconn of the old kiasyd or anything like that at all, but they were probably made to expand the history of the original kiasyd since...The maeghar are avoiding the shit out of them. Also remember that lore of the bloodlines is a book that is coming out that will have a write up of the kiasyd if i remember correctly</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? What's the point? Kyasid are an obscure snowflake bloodline that most likely doesn't hit double digits in numbers. They are less relevant to the setting than freaking Trujah or Old Clan Tzimisce. Why are Kyasid getting page after page of content instead of the real clans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:53:28-07:00","id":884879,"title":"","content":"Because the clans just got their own book and have the majority of the setting dedicated to them? The Kiasyd are among the four oldest bloodlines in the world..ignoring clans who have become a bloodline. The Baali True Brujah and the Nagaraja are the only three living bloodlines that out age them. They are also getting a write up so they stop being just this super obscure bloodline that are basically unplayable. If they weren't then doing all of this would have been pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:50:20-07:00","id":885010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=884879#post884879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the clans just got their own book and have the majority of the setting dedicated to them? The Kiasyd are among the four oldest bloodlines in the world..ignoring clans who have become a bloodline. The Baali True Brujah and the Nagaraja are the only three living bloodlines that out age them. They are also getting a write up so they stop being just this super obscure bloodline that are basically unplayable. If they weren't then doing all of this would have been pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Good point, good sir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:17:39-07:00","id":887182,"title":"","content":"Eh, the older members of the Old Clan Tzimisce probably predate the creation of the Nagaraja (and possibly the Trujah, depending on who's right about their origins), though the bloodline didn't seem to officially split off from the the main clan until the Dark Ages. Up to that point they were just Tzimisce that were more interested in hypnotism and magic than fleshcrafting serfs into furniture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:32:16-07:00","id":887246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860635-the-black-hand-a-guide-to-the-tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra?p=887182#post887182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, the older members of the Old Clan Tzimisce probably predate the creation of the Nagaraja (and possibly the Trujah, depending on who's right about their origins), though the bloodline didn't seem to officially split off from the the main clan until the Dark Ages. Up to that point they were just Tzimisce that were more interested in hypnotism and magic than fleshcrafting serfs into furniture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. I'm just guessing, but I think Caedus is thinking less of the clan variants like the Old Clan or the Assamite castes, and more of the bloodlines that are/have become something distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:36:40-07:00","id":888520,"title":"","content":"The Old clan as an organization is not older than the kiasyd and yes i was reffering to distinct bloodlines. Not clan variants or legacies...since it is honestly hard to say how old some of the older legacies are...like the Guruhi..THE GURUHI ARE THE LAND <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />...Joking aside I am actually kind of sad we did not see the impundulu or ramanaga in the hand since they both fit in it rather well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T10:24:48-07:00","id":1517216,"title":"","content":"Using my elder powers, I resurrect this thread to once again announce character sheets....<br /> <br /> Per a recent request I now have character sheets for Idran Itarajana Sorcerers that were mentioned in the V20 book 'Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra'!<br /> <br /> I hope you like them!<br /> <br /> <br /> You can download them from my site in the V20 section here: <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/wod.html#v20\" target=\"_blank\">https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/wod.html#v20</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Should you need them, here are some direct links:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-